/** Generated from the overhaul textbook. Re-run tools/import-overhaul-courses.mjs. Do not edit by hand. */
export default {"id":"note-level-12","number":12,"title":"Production Labs","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"12.1","modules":[{"id":"note-m-12-1-101","code":"12.1","title":"12.1","blurb":"12.1","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"note-l12-1-1","title":"12.1.1 — Tempo zone choice (cite only if using a sourced BPM range)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.1.1 — Tempo zone choice (cite only if using a sourced BPM range)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.1 — Lab: one-hour house sketch on Note</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Lock a tempo for this house-flavored hour using only Set Settings or a first Capture, without treating any BPM as a sourced house rule."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"This module is a timed sketch, not a house-production degree. Beatmaking with Ableton Note starts you with a working title, a prompt, a limitation, and an intention. It does not publish a genre BPM table."},{"type":"prose","html":"{type:'gap'} The extracts in this library do not state a house tempo range. Do not invent 120–128 or any other house number. You still choose a tempo because drums, Capture, and scenes sit on one grid."},{"type":"prose","html":"Tap the <strong>Set Settings</strong> icon to the right of the Set name and open <strong>Tempo</strong>. Three sourced controls live there: a coarse horizontal slider, <strong>±1 BPM</strong> arrows, and <strong>Tap Tempo</strong> (four taps set the tempo; further taps keep updating it). The FAQ also documents the other path: with transport stopped, play a phrase and Capture; Note extracts tempo from that performance. If you already decided a number, set it now so the first Capture does not overwrite it."},{"type":"prose","html":"Note 2.0.1 remembers the last used tempo when you create a new Set. Glance at the inherited number and change it if it is not the one you want. Earlier course drills that set 90, 120, or 140 on purpose are decision practice, not a claim that house equals 120."},{"type":"prose","html":"Musical reason: a one-hour sketch dies if you spend the first twenty minutes hunting a “correct” house BPM. Pick a playable number, write it down, and move to drums."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Tap <strong>+ New</strong>. Rename the Set with a working title that constrains the hour (Beatmaking: a title suggests sound).","Write one prompt and one limitation on paper (example limitation: no extra tracks until Scene 1 exists).","Tap <strong>Set Settings</strong> → <strong>Tempo</strong>.","Set a tempo you chose with the slider, then the ±1 arrows, or with four Tap Tempo taps.","Enable the metronome once, press <strong>Play</strong>, listen for four bars, then <strong>Stop</strong>. Confirm the number did not drift.","Close Set Settings. Reopen <strong>Tempo</strong> from memory and say the number out loud."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Do the extracts state a house BPM you must use? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. {type:'gap'} Sources document how to set tempo, not a house range.","What happens if transport is stopped and the first Capture happens before you set tempo? <strong>Answer:</strong> Note extracts tempo from that performance (Manual §8.1.1–8.1.2; FAQ tempo).","Where are the three manual tempo controls? <strong>Answer:</strong> Set Settings → Tempo: coarse slider, ±1 arrows, Tap Tempo."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §5.2 Tempo; §8.1.1–8.1.2 first Capture sets tempo","Note FAQ p.4 “How do I select the tempo of a Set?”","RN 2.0.1 last used tempo remembered","Beatmaking with Ableton Note: title, prompt, limitation, intention"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. New Set, working title, written prompt, chosen tempo logged on your notes page. Do not Capture drums yet."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-1-1</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-1-2","title":"12.1.2 — Drum Capture Fixed Length 1–2 bars","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.1.2 — Drum Capture Fixed Length 1–2 bars","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.1 — Lab: one-hour house sketch on Note</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Capture a 1- or 2-bar drum loop with Fixed Length so Scene 1 has a kick, snare, and hat you can explain."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Fixed Length Capture is the sourced drum factory for this lab. In Session View, tap <strong>Add Clip</strong> on the drum track. In Instrument View, tap the plus icon in the clip area and choose <strong>1</strong> or <strong>2</strong> bars. Play pads while the empty clip loops. Notes appear in the editor as outlines until you tap <strong>Add</strong>, which commits them."},{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking names the drum jobs without inventing Note devices: kick is the punchy pulse on the downbeat; snare answers on the backbeat; hats tell a story by skipping through note divisions. Use the default Drum Rack (16 pads, 4×4). Repeat is legal here: hold a hat pad and pick <strong>1/16</strong> or <strong>1/8</strong> from the Repeat submenu (1/4, 1/4T, 1/8, 1/8T, 1/16, 1/16T, 1/32, 1/32T, or OFF). Repeat works in Fixed Length."},{"type":"prose","html":"If transport was stopped and this is the first Capture, Note may extract tempo from your playing (Manual §8.1.1). You already chose a tempo in 12.1.1 — press Play first or accept that first-capture rule and check Tempo afterward."},{"type":"prose","html":"Keep the loop short. An 8-bar drum epic wastes the hour. Beatmaking’s 80/20 rule: the main parts arrive quickly; do not fine-tune until you decide the idea is worth it. Record first; evaluate later."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Open the house-lab Set from 12.1.1. Confirm tempo.","Tap <strong>Add Clip</strong> on the drum track. Tap the plus icon. Choose <strong>1</strong> or <strong>2</strong> bars.","Play a kick on downbeats and a snare on backbeats. Tap <strong>Add</strong>.","Overdub hats: with transport running, play hats (or hold Repeat 1/16), then tap <strong>Add</strong> again.","If a pass is wrong, tap <strong>X</strong> to clear uncommitted notes, then recapture. Quantize only if the grid helps; skip it if the feel is the point.","Return to Session. Launch the clip. From memory, say whether this clip is 1 or 2 bars and which pads you used."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["When do outlined notes become part of the clip? <strong>Answer:</strong> When you tap <strong>Add</strong> (Manual §8.1.1; Capture in Note, Fixed Length).","Which Repeat divisions are sourced? <strong>Answer:</strong> 1/4, 1/4T, 1/8, 1/8T, 1/16, 1/16T, 1/32, 1/32T, or OFF.","Why start drums at 1–2 bars instead of 16? <strong>Answer:</strong> Clips max at 16 bars, but Beatmaking wants the main parts fast; a short loop is enough to build scenes."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §8.1.1 Fixed Length; §8.1.3 Repeat","Capture in Note: Fixed Length 1/2/4/8 bars (manual also lists 16)","Beatmaking: kick, snare, hat; 80/20; record first","Note FAQ: MIDI recording happens via Capture"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. One 1- or 2-bar drum clip with kick, snare, and hats committed. No bass yet."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-1-2</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-1-3","title":"12.1.3 — Bass Capture Free Length over drums","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.1.3 — Bass Capture Free Length over drums","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.1 — Lab: one-hour house sketch on Note</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Capture a bass clip with Free Length while the drum loop runs, then state whether Create Clip followed the shortest-clip rule."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Free Length means you play without pre-adding a clip, then commit. Two transport states matter."},{"type":"prose","html":"If transport is <strong>stopped</strong>, you can play up to eight bars and tap <strong>Capture</strong>. The first-ever Capture with transport stopped also sets tempo — you already set tempo, so do not do this first capture stopped unless you want that rewrite."},{"type":"prose","html":"If transport is <strong>running</strong> and other clips exist, you play, then tap <strong>Create Clip</strong>. Newly captured clips have at least as many bars as the <strong>shortest clip already in the Set</strong> (Manual §8.1.2). Your drum clip is 1 or 2 bars, so a Free Length bass captured while drums loop will not be a surprise 16-bar epic unless a longer clip already exists."},{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking treats 808/bass as the tuning reference for the root of the song. Use the default bass track or any melodic bass preset. Long notes against the kick create motion. You do not need a sourced “808 device”; you need notes that sit under the drums."},{"type":"prose","html":"Play, listen, then Create Clip. If the buffer is wrong, tap <strong>X</strong> and play again. Capture Timeout (Preferences) clears the buffer after you stop playing when the option is on; it does not affect overdub into an existing clip."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Launch the drum clip from 12.1.2 so transport is running.","Open the bass track header (do not tap Add Clip).","Play a bass line for at least one loop of the drums.","Tap <strong>Create Clip</strong>. Check the new clip’s length against the drum clip.","If notes are late, open the MIDI Editor from Clip Preview and nudge or Quantize. If the idea is wrong, Delete the clip and recapture.","Mute and unmute the bass once. Confirm you can still name which notes are the root."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What button label appears when transport is running and clips already exist? <strong>Answer:</strong> <strong>Create Clip</strong>, not the stopped-transport <strong>Capture</strong> button (Manual §8.1.2).","How long is a new clip captured while other clips play? <strong>Answer:</strong> At least as many bars as the shortest existing clip.","Does Capture Timeout change overdub into an existing clip? <strong>Answer:</strong> No (Manual §2.4.2)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §8.1.2 Free Length; shortest-clip rule; §2.4.2 Capture Timeout","Capture in Note: Free Length; first capture tempo","Beatmaking: 808/bass as tuning reference","Note FAQ: MIDI via Capture; no MIDI file import"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One Free Length bass clip over the running drums. Write the clip length and the shortest existing clip length on your notes page."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-1-3</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-1-4","title":"12.1.4 — In Key chord stab","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.1.4 — In Key chord stab","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.1 — Lab: one-hour house sketch on Note</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Turn In Key on, pick a root and scale, and Capture a chord stab that cannot play out-of-scale notes on the melodic pads."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>In Key</strong> lives in <strong>Set Settings → Key &amp; Scale</strong>. It is off by default, so pads are chromatic (all twelve notes). Enable the switch, choose a root, then a scale type. Melodic pads snap to that scale. Preview pads in the same menu use whichever melodic instrument was last selected. If the Set has no melodic instrument, the In Key options are greyed out."},{"type":"prose","html":"Note 2.0.1 defaults new Sets to <strong>C Major</strong> and a piano layout for new melodic tracks. You may keep C Major or change the root. That is a version fact, not a house rule."},{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking: find three or four chords that sound nice together, loop them until they bore you, then switch. Add delay and reverb later if you want them to linger — this lesson is the stab, not the FX pair. A stab is a short chord, not a pad bed (pad beds belong to Module 12.3)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Use a melodic track (Drift, Wavetable, or Melodic Sampler). Keys layout with In Key on becomes equal rectangles of in-scale notes; with In Key off it is a chromatic piano. Pads are 5×5 by default. Capture Fixed Length 1 or 2 bars, or overdub into a new clip while drums and bass run."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Tap <strong>Set Settings → Key &amp; Scale</strong>. Turn <strong>In Key</strong> on. Choose a root and scale. Tap the preview pads.","Open a melodic track. Confirm pads or Keys only offer in-scale notes.","Play a two- or three-note stab on the downbeat. Capture it (Fixed Length plus icon, or Create Clip while transport runs).","Tap <strong>Add</strong> if you used Fixed Length.","Launch drums, bass, and the stab together. If a note fights the bass root, edit pitch in the MIDI Editor (transpose snaps to the scale when In Key is on).","From memory, say the root, the scale, and whether In Key was on."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What is the factory default for In Key? <strong>Answer:</strong> Off — chromatic (Manual §5.3). RN 2.0.1 then defaults new Sets to C Major.","When are Key &amp; Scale options greyed out? <strong>Answer:</strong> When no melodic instruments are in the Set.","What happens to melodic pads when In Key is on? <strong>Answer:</strong> They snap to the selected root and scale."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §5.3 Key &amp; Scale; §8.1.3 Keys layout","Note FAQ p.4 “How do I select the key and scale”","RN 2.0.1 C Major default; piano layout default","Beatmaking: 3–4 chords; delay/reverb to linger"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. One in-scale chord-stab clip launched with drums and bass. Write root + scale on the notes page."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-1-4</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-1-5","title":"12.1.5 — Scene 1 full / Scene 2 drop hats / Scene 3 add FX shot","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.1.5 — Scene 1 full / Scene 2 drop hats / Scene 3 add FX shot","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.1 — Lab: one-hour house sketch on Note</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Build three scenes from the same clips so form comes from density, not from a longer clip."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"A scene is a horizontal row of clips. Tap a scene number to launch every clip in that row. Show scene numbers with the <strong>Show/Hide Scene Numbers</strong> control at the bottom of Session View. Maximum <strong>eight</strong> scenes. Long-press a scene number to rearrange, duplicate, or delete."},{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking warns against an amazing 8-bar loop that spins forever. Start with a hook-like full scene, keep a verse-like scene sparser so a vocal could sit, and use a shot for excitement: a vocal phrase, a reverse cymbal, or a piano note with long reverb. You already have drums, bass, and a chord stab. That is enough for Scene 1."},{"type":"prose","html":"Scene 2 is the same idea with hats dropped — mute the drum track’s hats by capturing a drum variation without them, or Duplicate the drum clip, edit hats out, and place the thinner clip in Scene 2. Do not invent a mute-per-pad mixer; use clip contents and track <strong>M</strong> only as sourced."},{"type":"prose","html":"Scene 3 adds a shot. Duplicate a scene or add a clip on a free track (max <strong>8 tracks</strong>). A one-shot Melodic Sampler note, a Drum Rack crash, or a short recorded vocal (Level 9 path) all count. Reverse is available from RN 1.0.12 if your version includes it."},{"type":"prose","html":"Launch scenes, not just clips, so you hear form."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Turn <strong>Show/Hide Scene Numbers</strong> on.","Put drums, bass, and chord stab in <strong>Scene 1</strong>. Launch the scene number. That is the full row.","Long-press the Scene 1 number → <strong>Duplicate</strong> to create Scene 2, or copy clips down by long-press Duplicate on each clip.","In Scene 2, replace the drum clip with a version that has no hats (Duplicate clip + MIDI Editor delete, or a new 1-bar Capture).","Build <strong>Scene 3</strong> from Scene 1 plus one shot clip on a spare track or empty slot.","Launch 1, then 2, then 3. From memory, name what each scene withholds or adds."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["How do you launch every clip in a row at once? <strong>Answer:</strong> Tap the scene number (Manual §4.3).","What is the scene ceiling? <strong>Answer:</strong> Eight scenes per Set.","Why not just lengthen one clip to 16 bars? <strong>Answer:</strong> Form is scene density (Beatmaking sections). Clips still max at 16 bars."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §4.3 Scenes; §4.2 clip duplicate/delete","Beatmaking: chorus/hook, verse sparse, shots, avoid endless loop","RN 1.0.12 Reverse samples (if used for the shot)","FAQ: max 8 scenes"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Fifteen minutes. Three launchable scenes: full, hats dropped, shot added. Do not export yet."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-1-5</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-1-6","title":"12.1.6 — One automation (filter or delay)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.1.6 — One automation (filter or delay)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.1 — Lab: one-hour house sketch on Note</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Capture one filter or Delay automation into an existing clip so a solid line and a parameter dot prove it stored."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Automation in Note is Capture, not a separate record-arm. Transport <strong>must</strong> be running. Move a device or effect knob. A <strong>dotted</strong> line appears in Clip Preview. Tap <strong>Add</strong> to store it. The line turns <strong>solid</strong>. A <strong>dot</strong> appears on the automated parameter. You cannot <strong>Return to Default</strong> while that parameter is automated — Delete the automation first (parameter menu)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Pick one move that serves the three scenes. Opening a filter into Scene 1 or riding Delay feedback toward Scene 3 is enough. Each Track Preset has <strong>two</strong> effect slots (FX1 then FX2 on melodic tracks; Pad FX / Kit FX on Drum Rack). Delay and Auto Filter are sourced effect categories. Auto Filter arrives in Note 1.4; if your version lacks it, automate a filter knob on the instrument or a Delay parameter instead. {type:'gap'} Sources do not require a specific house filter frequency."},{"type":"prose","html":"Re-adjust and tap <strong>Add</strong> again to replace the curve. Tap <strong>X</strong> to keep the previous solid curve. <strong>Insert</strong> writes a straight line at the current value. <strong>Delete</strong> removes that parameter’s automation."},{"type":"prose","html":"One parameter. The hour is for a sketch, not a mix."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Launch Scene 1 so transport is running.","Open the chord or bass track. Show Delay or the instrument filter (or Auto Filter if present).","Move one knob through a loop. Confirm the dotted line in Clip Preview.","Tap <strong>Add</strong>. Confirm the line is solid and the parameter shows a dot.","Stop and play the clip. Watch the knob move by itself.","Open the parameter menu. Confirm <strong>Return to Default</strong> is greyed. Do not Delete unless the move is wrong."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Can you capture automation with transport stopped? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Transport must be running (Manual §7.5; Capture in Note).","What does a dotted line vs a solid line mean? <strong>Answer:</strong> Dotted = pending; solid = stored after <strong>Add</strong>.","Why is Return to Default greyed? <strong>Answer:</strong> The parameter is automated. Delete automation first."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §7.5 Automation; §7.5.1 Insert/Delete; §7.4 Delay, Auto Filter","Capture in Note: Automation pages","Note FAQ: “How do I record automation?” — via Capture","RN 1.4 Auto Filter"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. One stored automation on filter or Delay. Screenshot or write which parameter shows the dot."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-1-6</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-1-7","title":"12.1.7 — Export + optional Cloud","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.1.7 — Export + optional Cloud","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.1 — Lab: one-hour house sketch on Note</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Bounce the three-scene sketch to audio, then optionally upload the Set to Cloud or Share To… without treating Cloud as a backup."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Export Audio</strong> lives in <strong>Set Settings</strong>. It is greyed if the Set has no clips. The bounce is every scene <strong>top to bottom</strong>. The longest clip in a scene sets that scene’s length in the file. Formats: uncompressed <strong>WAV 48 kHz 16-bit</strong> or compressed <strong>M4A 48 kHz 32-bit</strong>. After render, a preview appears; <strong>Share</strong> sends the file to Files, AirDrop, or another app."},{"type":"prose","html":"Cloud is optional in this lesson and is <strong>transfer, not backup</strong>. Cloud holds <strong>eight</strong> Sets. Same Ableton account email as the Live license. Enable via Settings toggle, the library banner, or Set Options → <strong>Upload to Ableton Cloud</strong>. Local copy remains in Files → On My iPhone/iPad → Ableton Note → Projects. Uploads need Wi-Fi or allowed mobile data; they queue until a connection exists."},{"type":"prose","html":"If you share with someone who does not share your Cloud login, use <strong>Share To…</strong>. That creates an <strong>.ablbundle</strong> (Set + samples + metadata) that opens in Note or Live 11.2.5+."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not delete the local Set after upload. Do not expect a Live save to come back into Note."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Launch all three scenes once so you know the order is 1–2–3 top to bottom.","<strong>Set Settings → Export Audio</strong>. Choose WAV or M4A. Export. Listen to the preview.","Tap <strong>Share</strong> and save the bounce to Files.","Optional: Set Options → <strong>Upload to Ableton Cloud</strong>. Wait until the Set sits in the Cloud library section.","If Cloud is full (8), remove a Set you already archived via Share To…, then upload.","Confirm the Set is still in Local/Projects. Cloud is not the only copy."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What determines each scene’s length in the bounce? <strong>Answer:</strong> The longest clip in that scene (Manual §10.2).","How many Sets does Cloud hold? <strong>Answer:</strong> Eight (FAQ; RN 1.2 raised the cap from 5).","Can a collaborator without your Ableton login take the Set from your Cloud? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Use Share To… / .ablbundle (FAQ)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §5.4, §10.2 Export Audio; §10.1 Cloud","Note FAQ: Cloud 8 Sets; transfer not backup; Share To…","Sharing Note Sets KB","Note Compatibility: Live 11.2.5+"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One audio export saved to Files. Optional Cloud upload. Write format (WAV or M4A) on the notes page."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-1-7</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-1-8","title":"12.1.8 — Critique: what must move to Live next","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.1.8 — Critique: what must move to Live next","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.1 — Lab: one-hour house sketch on Note</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Judge the house sketch after a short delay and write only the jobs that Note cannot finish."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking separates making from judging. Put the Set away, even for a short walk. Ask: is any idea memorable? The 80/20 rule says you already have the main parts if they arrived quickly. Do not mix for another hour inside Note."},{"type":"prose","html":"Note is a Session-grid sketchbook. It is not mobile Live. Sourced ceilings that block a finished house record: <strong>8 tracks</strong>, <strong>8 scenes</strong>, clips <strong>max 16 bars</strong>, no Arrangement View, no MIDI file I/O, no AUv3, no pitch bend, Cloud <strong>Note → Live only</strong>. Sampler/Drum Rack transpose still couples speed (FAQ warp rule). Audio tracks in Note 2.0.1 can warp loops — that is a later version path, not a reason to stay in Note forever."},{"type":"prose","html":"What belongs in Live (sister course, not this lab): Arrangement View, deep device pages, third-party plugins, long-form arrangement, mix bus work beyond two Main FX. After you open the Set in Live 11.2.5+, <strong>Collect All and Save</strong> immediately so samples survive if you later remove the Cloud slot."},{"type":"prose","html":"Write three bullets: keep in Note, park, send to Live. If nothing is memorable, park the Set. Do not force a Live hand-off for a loop you already forgot."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Close Note for at least ten minutes (longer if you have it).","Reopen the Set. Launch Scene 1, 2, and 3 only. Do not add clips.","Write: working title, tempo you chose, root/scale, origin of each clip (Fixed vs Free vs edit).","Write three jobs that require Live (Arrangement, extra tracks, plugins, or warp-independent sampler work).","If the idea is a keeper, leave it Local and optionally in Cloud. If not, Share To… Files once, then you may delete later.","Stop. The hour is over."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Why delay the critique? <strong>Answer:</strong> Beatmaking: give space between create and judge; time / memorable test.","Can you finish the Live arrangement inside Note and send it back? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Live Sets cannot open in Note (FAQ; Manual §10.1).","What is the first Live command after opening a Note Set? <strong>Answer:</strong> Collect All and Save (Manual §10.1; FAQ Managing Files)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Beatmaking: delay, memorable, 80/20, finish later","Ableton Note Manual §10.1 one-way Cloud; Collect All and Save","Note FAQ: limits; no Live→Note; no MIDI I/O; warp/transpose on sampler path","RN 2.0.1 audio-track warp (contrast only)","Ableton Note.md: Note is not mobile Live; Session only"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes after a delay. One critique page: clip origins + three Live-only jobs + keep/park/send."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-1-8</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"note-m-12-2-102","code":"12.2","title":"12.2","blurb":"12.2","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"note-l12-2-1","title":"12.2.1 — Sparse drums first","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.2.1 — Sparse drums first","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.2 — Lab: trap/hip-hop mobile sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Capture a sparse drum clip first so the verse has space, using only kick, snare, and a few hats."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking’s verse is the storytelling section. Keep instrumentation sparse so a vocal could sit. That is the whole drum job in this lesson. Do not fill every 16th."},{"type":"prose","html":"{type:'gap'} Sources do not publish a trap BPM range. Set tempo the same way as 12.1.1: Set Settings → Tempo (slider, ±1, Tap Tempo) or accept first-Capture extraction. Do not invent 70/140."},{"type":"prose","html":"Start a new Set. Working title + intention (Beatmaking). Use the default Drum Rack. Fixed Length <strong>1</strong> or <strong>2</strong> bars. Kick on the downbeat, snare on the backbeat, hats only where they tell a story. Repeat is available but you do not have to use it yet (that is 12.2.3)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Max <strong>8 tracks</strong>. You will not need more than drums, bass, one texture, and maybe a hook layer for this whole module. Record first; do not mix."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Tap <strong>+ New</strong>. Name the Set. Set a tempo you chose. Write the number down.","<strong>Add Clip</strong> on the drum track. Plus icon → <strong>1</strong> or <strong>2</strong> bars.","Capture kick and snare only. Tap <strong>Add</strong>.","Add the fewest hats that still mark time. Tap <strong>Add</strong> again. If you overplayed, tap <strong>X</strong> before Add, or edit notes out in the MIDI Editor.","Launch the clip. Count the empty grid cells. If the loop feels busy, delete hats until it does not.","From memory, list which pads you used."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Why start sparse? <strong>Answer:</strong> Beatmaking: verse stays thin so a vocal can be heard; 80/20 — main parts first.","Must you use Repeat on this clip? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Repeat is optional and is the next lesson.","Is there a sourced trap tempo? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. {type:'gap'} Choose tempo with Set Settings."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §8.1.1 Fixed Length; §4.1 max 8 tracks","Beatmaking: verse sparse; kick/snare/hat roles; record first","Note FAQ: tempo via Set Settings or first Capture"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. One sparse 1–2 bar drum clip. No bass until 12.2.2."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-2-1</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-2-2","title":"12.2.2 — 808-style long notes on a melodic bass preset","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.2.2 — 808-style long notes on a melodic bass preset","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.2 — Lab: trap/hip-hop mobile sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Capture long bass notes on a melodic bass preset so the low end is a tuned line, not a second kick pattern."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking: the original 808 was a synthesized kick that got extended, detuned, and turned into a tuned bass line. It sets the root of the song. Note does not ship a device labeled “808” in the extracts. Use a <strong>melodic bass preset</strong> (default bass track, Drift, or Wavetable bass). Long notes. Gate/length in the MIDI Editor if a note dies early."},{"type":"prose","html":"Transpose on <strong>Sampler / Drum Rack</strong> also changes playback speed (FAQ: warp not available on that path). If you put a kick sample on Melodic Sampler and transpose it, it will speed up or slow down. Note <strong>2.0.1 audio tracks</strong> warp loops so tempo and pitch are independent — that is a different path. For this lab, prefer a synth bass preset so pitch is just pitch."},{"type":"prose","html":"In Key on (Set Settings → Key &amp; Scale) keeps the line in scale. Play held notes against the sparse drums. Free Length while drums run: <strong>Create Clip</strong>; length follows the shortest existing clip. Or Fixed Length 1–2 bars and drag note ends longer."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not stack five bass tracks. Eight-track ceiling is a real limit."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Launch the sparse drums. Open the bass track.","Browse a bass-category Track Preset. Play pads. Tap <strong>Done</strong>.","Turn <strong>In Key</strong> on if you want the line locked to a root.","Play long notes (one per bar or half-bar). <strong>Create Clip</strong> or Fixed Length + <strong>Add</strong>.","In the MIDI Editor, drag the right edge of notes so they sustain. Check velocity.","Solo drums + bass. Confirm the bass names the root you hear."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Does Note’s FAQ name an “808 device”? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Beatmaking describes 808 as a tuned bass idea. Use a melodic bass preset.","What does Transpose do on Sampler/Drum Rack? <strong>Answer:</strong> It also changes playback speed (FAQ warp rule).","How do you lengthen a captured note? <strong>Answer:</strong> MIDI Editor: drag the note’s right edge (Manual §8.2)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Beatmaking: 808/bass as extended, detuned, tuned reference","Note FAQ: warp not on sampler path; transpose couples speed","RN 2.0.1 audio-track warp (contrast)","Ableton Note Manual §8.1.2 Free Length; §8.2 note length"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One long-note bass clip under the sparse drums. Write the root note you used."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-2-2</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-2-3","title":"12.2.3 — Hat Repeat performance","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.2.3 — Hat Repeat performance","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.2 — Lab: trap/hip-hop mobile sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Perform hat motion with Repeat while a clip loops, then commit only the pass you want."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking: hats are where you skip through note divisions to tell a story. Pitch modulation adds style — Drum Sampler <strong>Transpose</strong> / <strong>Detune</strong> and page-2 FX exist, but this lesson is Repeat."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Repeat</strong> sits in Pad Performance Options (icon left of / below the pads). Divisions: <strong>1/4, 1/4T, 1/8, 1/8T, 1/16, 1/16T, 1/32, 1/32T</strong>, or <strong>OFF</strong>. Hold a pad; notes fire at that rate. Switch divisions while holding. Works in <strong>Pads</strong> and <strong>Single</strong>, and in both Fixed and Free Capture."},{"type":"prose","html":"For a hook layer, overdub Repeat hats into a <strong>Duplicate</strong> of the sparse drum clip so the verse clip stays thin. Duplicate Clip in Instrument View writes the copy to the next slot and switches playback to it. That is your hook drum clip."},{"type":"prose","html":"Single layout: select the hat pad first, then Single — upper half is higher velocity, lower half is lower. Useful for ghost motion. Do not Quantize a Repeat performance unless the rolls sound sloppy; Repeat is already on a grid."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Open the drum track. Duplicate the sparse clip into the next scene slot (or next clip down the track).","Open Pad Performance Options → <strong>Repeat</strong>. Choose <strong>1/16</strong>.","With transport running, hold the hat pad for a bar, then switch to <strong>1/32</strong> for a short roll. Tap <strong>Add</strong>.","Switch Repeat to <strong>OFF</strong>. Play one off-grid gap if you want space.","If the buffer is wrong, <strong>X</strong> and recapture. Leave the original sparse clip untouched.","Launch sparse clip, then the Repeat clip. Name the divisions you used."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["List the sourced Repeat divisions. <strong>Answer:</strong> 1/4, 1/4T, 1/8, 1/8T, 1/16, 1/16T, 1/32, 1/32T, or OFF.","Does Repeat work only in Fixed Length? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. It works in Fixed and Free (Capture in Note; Manual §8.1.3).","Why duplicate before the hat performance? <strong>Answer:</strong> So the verse clip stays sparse (Beatmaking verse vs hook)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §8.1.3 Repeat; Duplicate Clip","Capture in Note: Note Repeat page","Beatmaking: hats skip divisions; hook vs verse"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. One hook drum clip with a Repeat hat pass committed. Verse clip still sparse."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-2-3</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-2-4","title":"12.2.4 — Sample a voice note or room tone as texture","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.2.4 — Sample a voice note or room tone as texture","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.2 — Lab: trap/hip-hop mobile sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Record or import one environmental or voice sample onto a Drum Rack pad or Melodic Sampler and place it as a shot."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking shots: a vocal phrase, reverse cymbal, or piano with long reverb so the loop is not boring. Note records audio into <strong>Drum Rack</strong> or <strong>Melodic Sampler</strong>. Tap the track header, load Drum Rack or Sampler, select a pad (Drum Rack) or tap <strong>Record Sample</strong> (Sampler). The red square is the recording indicator; tap it to stop. Grant microphone access in iOS Settings → Privacy → Microphone if prompted. The orange mic icon is expected (FAQ)."},{"type":"prose","html":"You can also import <strong>WAV, AIFF, M4A, MP3</strong> (M4A/MP3 convert to WAV) via AirDrop or Share. Cloud warns around <strong>100 MB</strong> of sample data; samples over 100 MB cannot be imported (RN 1.0.6)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Resample (long-press the mic icon) records Note’s output — useful later, not required here. Transpose on this sampler path <strong>couples speed</strong> (FAQ). If the voice note plays too fast when pitched, leave Transpose at 0 or use a Note 2.x audio track (warped loops) if your version has it."},{"type":"prose","html":"Keep the sample as texture: one pad, one clip, one scene. Save the sample if you want it in User Library → Recordings."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Add or select a Sampler or Drum Rack track (stay under 8 tracks).","Record a short voice note or room tone, or import a file with Share/AirDrop.","Stop on the red square. Crop start if needed (drag waveform / start marker; RN 1.7.2+ markers).","Capture a clip that triggers the pad once per 2 or 4 bars, or place the note in the MIDI Editor.","Put that clip in the hook scene only, or in a third scene as a shot.","Listen with drums and bass. If it masks the vocal-space verse, remove it from the sparse scene."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Where can you record a sample? <strong>Answer:</strong> Into a Drum Rack pad or Melodic Sampler (Working with Samples; FAQ).","What does Transpose do to this sample? <strong>Answer:</strong> It also changes speed on the sampler path (FAQ). 2.x audio tracks differ.","Is the orange mic icon a fault? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Note accesses the mic by default (FAQ)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Working with Samples in Note: record, import, resample","Note FAQ: sample record; import formats; orange mic; transpose/speed","RN 1.0.6 100 MB; RN 1.7.2 start/end markers","Beatmaking: shots / vocal phrase"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One recorded or imported texture clip in the hook or shot scene only."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-2-4</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-2-5","title":"12.2.5 — Groove Amount experiment","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.2.5 — Groove Amount experiment","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.2 — Lab: trap/hip-hop mobile sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"A/B the same hat pattern at Groove Amount 0 and a higher setting so you can hear what the global control does."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Groove Amount</strong> lives in <strong>Set Settings</strong> (FAQ; added with global groove in RN <strong>1.0.15</strong>). Per-clip swing exists in that same release. {type:'gap'} The extracts do not publish the exact per-clip swing UI labels or numeric scale beyond “Groove Amount.” Teach the menu you actually see; do not invent percentages."},{"type":"prose","html":"Groove is not Quantize. Quantize pulls notes to a grid (Instrument View Quantize button; amount control from RN 1.0.15). Groove Amount adds feel on top of what is already in the clips. If you Quantize hats to 100% and then raise Groove, you are asking the Set-level control to humanize a rigid clip. If you leave Repeat hats unquantized, Groove still applies globally."},{"type":"prose","html":"This experiment needs one clip you already like (the Repeat hat clip). Do not rebuild the beat. Change only Groove Amount, listen, write what you hear, then decide a setting for the rest of the lab."},{"type":"prose","html":"If your Note version is older than 1.0.15, this control is absent. Record the version from Settings → Help and skip the comparison."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Check Settings → <strong>Help</strong> for the Note version. If older than 1.0.15, stop and log a gap.","Launch the hat-heavy clip. Set Settings → <strong>Groove Amount</strong> → <strong>0</strong>. Listen for 8 bars.","Raise Groove Amount. Listen to the same 8 bars. Do not change notes.","Toggle back to 0 once. Choose the setting you will keep.","If a per-clip swing control is visible on the clip, try it on the hat clip only, then return it if you cannot describe the change.","Write: version, Groove Amount kept, one sentence on feel vs Quantize."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Where is Groove Amount? <strong>Answer:</strong> Set Settings (FAQ; Manual-era Set Settings; RN 1.0.15).","Does Groove replace Repeat? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Repeat writes notes; Groove Amount is a Set-level feel control.","What if your version predates 1.0.15? <strong>Answer:</strong> The control is not there. Log version and skip."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ p.4 “Can I adjust swing or groove?”","RN 1.0.15 Global Groove Amount + per-clip swing; Quantisation amount","Ableton Note Manual §5 Set Settings","Beatmaking: hat divisions tell a story (feel, not extra tracks)"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Six minutes. Two listens (0 vs higher) on the same clip. Keep one Groove Amount for the Set."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-2-5</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-2-6","title":"12.2.6 — Two scenes: verse sparse / hook fuller","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.2.6 — Two scenes: verse sparse / hook fuller","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.2 — Lab: trap/hip-hop mobile sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Launch a two-scene sketch whose verse is thin and whose hook is denser, staying under eight tracks."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking: chorus/hook has a memorable melody and rhythm; verse stays sparse for the story (or a rap). Intro/outro can add a part every 1, 2, or 4 bars — optional here. You already have the clips: sparse drums, long bass, Repeat-hat drums, texture shot."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Scene 1 = verse:</strong> sparse drums + bass. No Repeat hats, no vocal shot (or the shot at very low density). <strong>Scene 2 = hook:</strong> Repeat-hat drums + bass + stab or texture. Tap scene numbers to launch whole rows."},{"type":"prose","html":"Stay under <strong>8 tracks</strong> and <strong>8 scenes</strong>. Do not lengthen clips toward 16 bars to fake form. Duplicate scenes or clips (long-press) rather than recapturing everything."},{"type":"prose","html":"Export is optional. The practice for this module is one trap-flavored sketch under 8 tracks. Critique after a delay (Beatmaking). If nothing is memorable, park it."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Show scene numbers.","Scene 1: sparse drum clip + bass only. Launch the scene number.","Scene 2: hook drum clip + bass + texture or a short melodic hook. Launch it.","Play 1 then 2 then 1. Confirm the verse still has air.","Mute one hook layer with <strong>M</strong>. If the hook still works, you may delete that track and stay leaner.","Write a two-line map: Scene 1 contents / Scene 2 contents."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["How do you switch verse to hook in one tap? <strong>Answer:</strong> Tap the scene number for that row (Manual §4.3).","What is the track ceiling? <strong>Answer:</strong> Eight (FAQ; Manual §4.1).","Why not make one 16-bar clip that contains both sections? <strong>Answer:</strong> Form is scenes (Beatmaking; clip max 16 bars is a ceiling, not a song form)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §4.3 Scenes; §4.1 tracks","Beatmaking: verse sparse, hook memorable, shots","Note FAQ: 8 tracks, 8 scenes, 16-bar clips","Module 12.2 practice: one trap-flavored sketch under 8 tracks"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Twelve minutes. Two launchable scenes. Stop. Delay before you judge the sketch."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-2-6</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"note-m-12-3-103","code":"12.3","title":"12.3","blurb":"12.3","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"note-l12-3-1","title":"12.3.1 — Drift or Wavetable pad macros","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.3.1 — Drift or Wavetable pad macros","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.3 — Lab: ambient / pad sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Load a Drift or Wavetable pad preset and learn its macros so later automation has named knobs."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"A Track Preset is an instrument plus <strong>two</strong> audio effects. <strong>Drift</strong> is subtractive; <strong>Wavetable</strong> uses wavetable oscillators. Parameters on screen differ per preset — do not expect a universal panel. Macros are the knobs you see first. Full Drift extra pages (Osc, Filter, Env, LFO, Mod, Global) are a purchase/restore path in the manual; FAQ also says there are currently no IAPs. {type:'gap'} If your storefront shows a Drift unlock and FAQ still says no IAP, teach only the knobs you can actually turn."},{"type":"prose","html":"Wavetable-from-Note in Live Lite/Intro/Standard becomes a <strong>locked rack</strong> (macros only). Full Wavetable is Suite or a Pack (Using Note Presets in Live). That matters later, not for this pad."},{"type":"prose","html":"Browse pad-like presets (slow envelopes). Attack and release macros, filter, and LFO are typical — but cite only what that preset shows. Double-tap a knob to reset. RN 2.0.1: tap a visual control to enter focused single-parameter mode; iPad shows visual + dials."},{"type":"prose","html":"Working title + intention: this sketch is one scene that will evolve by automation (12.3.5). No drum fill contest."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>+ New</strong>. Name an ambient working title. Set a slow tempo you chose (no sourced ambient BPM).","Open a melodic track. Browse Drift or Wavetable. Preview pads. <strong>Done</strong>.","Write the visible macro names. Turn each one, then double-tap to reset.","Capture a long chord or single held note (Fixed Length 4 or 8 bars, or Free Length stopped — up to 8 bars).","Save a user preset if you changed macros (asterisk → Save in browser).","From memory, list three macros you will automate later."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["How many audio effect slots does a Track Preset have? <strong>Answer:</strong> Two (Manual §7.1 / §7.4).","Are Wavetable’s deep pages available in Live Standard after a Note hand-off? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Locked rack; macros only (Using Note Presets in Live).","Do all Drift presets show the same knobs? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Default subset differs per preset (Manual §7.2.1)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §7.1 Track Presets; §7.2.1 Drift; §7.2.4 Wavetable","Using Note Presets in Live: locked Wavetable rack","Note FAQ: IAP line (conflict vs manual Drift purchase → gap)","RN 2.0.1 focused parameter mode","Beatmaking: intention; delay-before-judge"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One pad clip + written macro list. No field recording yet."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-3-1</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-3-2","title":"12.3.2 — Long reverb + delay (careful mud)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.3.2 — Long reverb + delay (careful mud)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.3 — Lab: ambient / pad sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Load Reverb and Delay on the pad track and set them so the tail lingers without hiding the chord."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Melodic Track Presets run <strong>FX1 then FX2</strong> in series. Swap an effect by tapping its name and picking a category: <strong>Reverb</strong> (algorithmic space) and <strong>Delay</strong> (time, filter, LFO options). Beatmaking says add delay and reverb so chords linger — and warns that leftover mud is your problem, not a new effect."},{"type":"prose","html":"You have only two slots on the track. Main track can hold up to <strong>two</strong> Main FX (RN 1.0.15+). Putting Reverb on Main and Delay on the track (or the reverse) is a sourced routing choice. Drum Rack Pad FX has <strong>Send Amount</strong>; this pad track does not — wet/dry lives on the effect knobs you actually see."},{"type":"prose","html":"There is no sourced “mud meter.” Use mixer volume, mute, and your ears. Double-tap a knob to reset. If the tail never decays, shorten Decay/Mix on Reverb or Feedback/Mix on Delay. Do not add a third track of the same pad to “make it bigger.”"},{"type":"prose","html":"Auto Filter (1.4+) can sit in a slot instead of one of these if the wash is too wide — but then you lose a slot. Choose."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Open the pad Track Preset. Tap FX1 name → <strong>Reverb</strong> → a long preset → <strong>Done</strong>.","Tap FX2 name → <strong>Delay</strong> → <strong>Done</strong>.","Launch the pad clip. Lower track volume if the tail clips the Main.","Reset one knob (double-tap), then set Mix/Decay by ear until you can still name the chord.","Optional: move one effect to Main (Main FX, version-aware) and compare.","Write which slot holds Reverb and which holds Delay."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["In what order do FX1 and FX2 run? <strong>Answer:</strong> FX1 first, then FX2 (Manual §7.4).","How many Main FX can a Set have from 1.0.15? <strong>Answer:</strong> Up to two.","Why not add a second pad track for “more reverb”? <strong>Answer:</strong> Eight-track ceiling; two FX slots already wash the sound; Beatmaking 80/20."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §7.4 Audio Effects; Reverb; Delay","RN 1.0.15 Main FX (up to 2)","Beatmaking: delay and reverb to linger"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. Reverb + Delay on the pad. Chord still identifiable. Write slot order."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-3-2</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-3-3","title":"12.3.3 — Slow automation of filter or wavetable macros","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.3.3 — Slow automation of filter or wavetable macros","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.3 — Lab: ambient / pad sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Capture one slow filter or Wavetable/Drift macro move so the pad clip changes over its own loop."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"This lab’s arrangement is automation, not extra scenes (that climax is 12.3.5). Transport running. Move one macro slowly across a 4- or 8-bar clip. Dotted line in Clip Preview → <strong>Add</strong> → solid line + parameter dot."},{"type":"prose","html":"Slow means one gesture per loop, not a filter twitch every beat. If the clip is only 1 bar, Duplicate Loop / extend toward 4 or 8 (max <strong>16 bars</strong>) so the move has time. Insert writes a straight line if you want a simple rise."},{"type":"prose","html":"Wavetable and Drift macros are the safe targets because they travel to Live as the Note surface (locked Wavetable rack in non-Suite Live). Do not automate a Suite-only page you cannot see."},{"type":"prose","html":"You may capture several parameters in one <strong>Add</strong>. This lesson asks for one. Re-Add replaces the curve; <strong>X</strong> keeps the old solid line. Delete from the parameter menu if you need Return to Default back."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Launch the pad clip. Confirm transport is running.","Choose one macro (filter, wavetable position, or a labeled macro from 12.3.1).","Move it slowly for one full loop. Check the dotted line.","Tap <strong>Add</strong>. Confirm solid line and dot.","Listen without touching the knob. The value must move by itself.","If the move is too fast, Delete automation, lengthen the clip, and recapture a slower gesture."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What must be true before automation Capture works? <strong>Answer:</strong> Transport is running (Manual §7.5).","What does a second Add do? <strong>Answer:</strong> Updates the stored automation for the parameters you moved.","Why lengthen the clip for a slow move? <strong>Answer:</strong> A 1-bar loop repeats the gesture every bar; 4–8 bars give the rise time. Max 16 bars."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §7.5 Automation; §8.2.4 loop/clip length","Capture in Note: Automation","Using Note Presets in Live: Note macros survive as the Live surface","Note FAQ: automation via Capture; 16-bar max"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One slow stored macro automation. Write the parameter name."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-3-3</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-3-4","title":"12.3.4 — Field recording bed under pad","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.3.4 — Field recording bed under pad","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.3 — Lab: ambient / pad sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Record a room or outdoor bed into Sampler or a Drum pad and sit it under the pad clip without stealing the chord."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Note’s job is sampling your environment (FAQ; Manual welcome). Record into <strong>Melodic Sampler</strong> or a <strong>Drum Rack</strong> pad. Headphones: prefer wired (Bluetooth 34–200 ms vs wired 5–10 ms). Pre-2.x <strong>Monitor Audio Input</strong> lives in Preferences and monitors when headphones are connected. Note 2.x removes that Settings toggle; monitoring is enabled from the track / empty sampler / audio clip (RN 2.0.1)."},{"type":"prose","html":"If you load the bed on Melodic Sampler, C3 is original pitch; other pads transpose <strong>and</strong> change speed (FAQ). For a bed that must stay in time, either leave Transpose at 0 on the sampler path or, on <strong>Note 2.0+</strong>, use an <strong>Audio</strong> track whose loops are warped (tempo and pitch independent). Version-gate that choice."},{"type":"prose","html":"Keep gain reasonable (waveform drag +24 to −70 dB in the manual sample view). Cloud 100 MB warning still applies if you later upload. One bed clip under the pad is enough. Mixer volume and <strong>M</strong> control the blend."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Add a Sampler, Drum Rack, or (2.x) Audio track. Stay under 8 tracks.","Record a 5–10 second room tone or outdoor bed. Stop on the red square.","If using 2.x Audio: confirm the loop warps when you change Set tempo by ±1.","If using Sampler: keep Transpose at 0. Place a long note or loop the clip.","Launch pad + bed. Lower the bed until the chord is still the subject.","Write: device path (Sampler vs Drum pad vs Audio) and Note version."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Does Transpose on Sampler keep duration? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Speed changes too (FAQ). 2.x audio tracks are the warped exception.","Where did input monitoring move in 2.x? <strong>Answer:</strong> Into the track / empty sampler / audio clip. Settings toggle removed (RN 2.0.1).","Why wired headphones while recording? <strong>Answer:</strong> Bluetooth latency 34–200 ms vs wired 5–10 ms (Bluetooth KB)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Working with Samples in Note; Manual §9","Note FAQ: record samples; transpose/speed; orange mic","RN 2.0.1 audio tracks warped; monitoring moved","Bluetooth Headphones and Latency in Note","Beatmaking: environmental texture as a shot/bed"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Twelve minutes. One field-recording bed under the pad. Version and path logged."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-3-4</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-3-5","title":"12.3.5 — Single scene evolving via automation only","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.3.5 — Single scene evolving via automation only","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.3 — Lab: ambient / pad sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Leave the sketch on one scene and make the arrangement from stored automation, not from extra rows."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Module practice: one ambient sketch where automation is the arrangement. You may use up to eight scenes, but this drill forbids adding Scene 2. Form comes from knobs you already captured (filter/macros, Delay mix, Reverb, bed gain if it is a device parameter)."},{"type":"prose","html":"If you need a second move, capture it on the <strong>same</strong> clips. Multi-parameter <strong>Add</strong> is legal. Insert a straight-line rise across the 8- or 16-bar clip. You cannot Return to Default on an automated knob; Delete first if a move is wrong."},{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking still applies: delay the critique; memorable wins. An endless single scene is the failure mode the Beatmaking extract warns about for songs — here it is a deliberate constraint. If the result is only a pretty loop, write that honestly. Live Arrangement View is where a long-form ambient piece grows (sister course)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Export optional. Stay under 8 tracks."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Delete or ignore any Scene 2 you started. One row only.","Lengthen the pad clip toward 8 bars if the automation has no room (max 16).","Capture or update one additional slow move (Delay mix, Reverb, or a second macro).","Launch the single scene. Do not touch knobs. Listen twice.","Write a time map: “bars 1–4 filter closed; bars 5–8 open,” using only stored automation.","Stop adding clips."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What is the arrangement in this Set? <strong>Answer:</strong> Stored automation on one scene’s clips, not extra scenes.","Can you reset an automated macro with double-tap Return to Default? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. The option is greyed until you Delete automation.","Is a one-scene sketch a finished song? <strong>Answer:</strong> Not required. Beatmaking: sketch first; Live Arrangement is a later job."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §7.5 Automation; §4.3 Scenes (unused on purpose)","Capture in Note: Automation","Beatmaking: delay-before-judge; loop vs sections","Ableton Note.md: no Arrangement View in Note","Module 12.3 practice note"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One scene, two stored moves, written bar map. No Scene 2."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-3-5</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"note-m-12-4-104","code":"12.4","title":"12.4","blurb":"12.4","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"note-l12-4-1","title":"12.4.1 — Import or record a loop","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.4.1 — Import or record a loop","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.4 — Lab: sample-chop sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Get one loop into a Drum Rack pad or Sampler so the next lesson can slice or assign it."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Two sourced inbound paths: <strong>record</strong> into Drum Rack / Melodic Sampler, or <strong>import</strong> WAV, AIFF, M4A, MP3 (M4A/MP3 → WAV) via AirDrop or Share. Files land under Libraries → User Library → <strong>Imported</strong>, or Current Set → <strong>Recordings</strong>."},{"type":"prose","html":"RN <strong>1.7.2</strong> adds External Folders (anywhere on the device; iCloud Drive download). RN <strong>1.0.15</strong> adds video-audio import (crop via Imported folder). Use those if your version has them."},{"type":"prose","html":"On <strong>Note 2.0+</strong>, Session <strong>+</strong> on an Audio track can <strong>record or load</strong> a sample; those loops are <strong>warped</strong>. Pre-2.x, a recorded loop on Sampler/Drum Rack is <strong>not</strong> independently warped. If the loop was recorded at a different tempo, transpose will also change speed (FAQ). Either match Set tempo to the loop (Tap Tempo / first Capture) or wait for Slice and live with the FAQ rule."},{"type":"prose","html":"100 MB Cloud warning; files larger than 100 MB cannot be imported (RN 1.0.6). Grant mic access if you record."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>+ New</strong>. Name the chop Set. Set tempo only if you already know the loop’s tempo; otherwise wait.","Import a loop (Share/AirDrop/External folder) <strong>or</strong> record a loop into Sampler or a Drum pad.","Confirm you hear it at Transpose 0.","If it rushes or drags against the metronome, either change Set tempo or note that warp is unavailable on this path.","Save the sample if you need it in other Sets (Save Sample).","Write: source (record vs import), format, Note version, warp path (sampler vs 2.x audio)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Which import formats are sourced? <strong>Answer:</strong> WAV, AIFF, M4A, MP3 (M4A/MP3 convert to WAV).","Can you warp a Drum Rack sample in pre-2.x Note? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. FAQ: warping not available; transpose changes speed.","What happens at 100 MB? <strong>Answer:</strong> Warning; larger samples cannot be imported or selected (RN 1.0.6)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Working with Samples in Note; Manual §9","Note FAQ: import formats; warp/transpose","RN 1.0.6 100 MB; 1.0.15 video import; 1.7.2 external folders; 2.0.1 audio load/record","Beatmaking: start with a limitation (one loop)"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One loop on a pad or Sampler, notes page filled. Do not slice yet."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-4-1</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-4-2","title":"12.4.2 — Slice to Drum pads (1.7.2+) or manual pad assignment","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.4.2 — Slice to Drum pads (1.7.2+) or manual pad assignment","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.4 — Lab: sample-chop sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Split the loop across Drum pads using Slice (1.7.2+) or by loading the same sample onto pads with different start points."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Note 1.7.2</strong> adds <strong>Sample Slicing</strong>: slice a sample to individual Drum Sampler pads, with start/end markers and per-slice markers. Choke group on sliced pads is in the later sample-options path (course Level 9). Check Settings → Help. If you are below 1.7.2, Slice is absent."},{"type":"prose","html":"Manual assignment still works on every version: copy/load the loop onto several pads, then drag each pad’s start (and, from 1.7.2, dedicated start/stop markers). Double-tap zooms to the selected range (1.7.2). Crop and save when start/end change (1.7.3)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not invent Live’s “Slice to New MIDI Track” dialog. Ableton Note.md’s older community notes said chopping was manual — that is historical. 1.7.2 is the version gate."},{"type":"prose","html":"Keep one Drum Rack. Sixteen pads. Choke (one group per rack) if you want chops to mute each other."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Read the Note version. If ≥ 1.7.2, open the loop pad’s sample options and use <strong>Slice</strong> to pads. If not, load the loop onto 4–8 empty pads.","Adjust per-pad start (and end if markers exist) so each pad is a different chop.","Enable <strong>Choke</strong> if you want monophonic chops.","Play the pads. You should hear different slices, not eight copies of bar 1.","Save slices if you need them outside this Set.","Write: Slice vs manual, version, how many pads."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Which release adds Slice to Drum pads? <strong>Answer:</strong> Note 1.7.2 (RN).","What is the manual fallback? <strong>Answer:</strong> Same sample on multiple pads with different start points.","How many Choke groups does a Drum Rack have? <strong>Answer:</strong> One (Manual §9.2)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["RN 1.7.2 Sample Slicing; start/stop markers; 1.7.3 crop/save","Ableton Note Manual §9 Sample Tab / Sample Options; Choke","Working with Samples in Note"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Twelve minutes. At least four distinct chops on pads. Version logged."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-4-2</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-4-3","title":"12.4.3 — Re-sequence with Capture/editor","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.4.3 — Re-sequence with Capture/editor","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.4 — Lab: sample-chop sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Perform a new order of chops with Capture, then fix timing or velocity in the MIDI Editor."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The loop’s original order is not the song. Play pads in a new order. Fixed Length 1–2 bars is enough for a chop groove. Free Length while a metronome or a kick clip runs uses <strong>Create Clip</strong> and the shortest-clip rule."},{"type":"prose","html":"MIDI Editor: tap Clip Preview. Tap a grid cell to add a note, tap a note to delete, drag length, long-press to select, pinch to zoom. Paint consecutive drum notes. <strong>16 Pitches</strong> (1.3+) retunes a drum note if you need a chop at another pitch — remember sampler transpose couples speed."},{"type":"prose","html":"Quantize after Capture if the performance is late. Amount control exists from RN 1.0.15. Do not Quantize away a swing you already like (Groove Amount is Set-level)."},{"type":"prose","html":"This is still one Drum Rack track. Scenes come later if you want a drop. Max 16 bars per clip."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Add Clip</strong> on the sliced Drum Rack. Plus icon → 1 or 2 bars.","Play a new pad order (not the original loop). Tap <strong>Add</strong>.","Open the MIDI Editor. Delete doubles. Nudge late hits or Quantize.","Adjust velocity on the right handle or Velocity tab so chops are not all equal.","Launch the clip. Confirm it does not merely replay the imported loop.","From memory, tap the pad order you used."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["How do you open the editor? <strong>Answer:</strong> Tap Clip Preview in Instrument View (Manual; FAQ).","What does 16 Pitches change? <strong>Answer:</strong> The pitch of a drum note (RN 1.3 / Manual MIDI Editor). Speed still follows transpose on the sampler path.","When should you skip Quantize? <strong>Answer:</strong> When the feel (or Groove Amount) is the point."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §8.1 Capture; §8.2 MIDI Editor","RN 1.3 MIDI Editor feature set; 16 Pitches","Capture in Note: editing tabs","Note FAQ: editor via Instrument View; no MIDI file I/O"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One re-sequenced chop clip that is not the original loop order."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-4-3</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-4-4","title":"12.4.4 — FX Type Punch/FM/8-Bit on one slice","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.4.4 — FX Type Punch/FM/8-Bit on one slice","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.4 — Lab: sample-chop sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Put Punch, FM, or 8-Bit on a single Drum pad so one chop is colored and the others stay dry."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Drum Sampler page 2 (RN <strong>1.2</strong>) holds playback FX and an X/Y pad. Sourced <strong>FX Type</strong> list: Stretch, Loop, Pitch Env, <strong>Punch</strong>, <strong>8-Bit</strong>, <strong>FM</strong>, Ring Mod, Sub Osc, Noise. This lesson uses Punch, FM, or 8-Bit only."},{"type":"prose","html":"Select the pad first. Page 1 is Transpose, filter, envelopes. Page 2 is the FX Type and X/Y. Pad FX (third tab) is a different slot — a full effect with <strong>Send Amount</strong>. Kit FX hits the whole rack. Color <strong>one</strong> slice so the re-sequence still reads as a kit, not a smashed loop."},{"type":"prose","html":"If your version is below 1.2, page 2 is missing. Log the version and use Pad FX (Redux is the bit-crusher category) on that pad’s send instead. That is a fallback, not the same control."},{"type":"prose","html":"Velocity can modulate FX1/FX2 on the pad (Manual Drum Sampler). Optional."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Select one chop pad — not the whole rack.","Open Drum Sampler page 2 (1.2+). Set <strong>FX Type</strong> to Punch, FM, or 8-Bit.","Move the X/Y pad. Play only that pad.","Play the re-sequence clip. Only that slice should change character.","If the whole kit changed, you edited Kit FX. Undo and return to the pad’s FX Type.","Write: pad name/sample, FX Type, version."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Which release adds Drum Sampler page 2 + X/Y? <strong>Answer:</strong> Note 1.2 (RN).","Name three sourced FX Types this lesson allows. <strong>Answer:</strong> Punch, FM, 8-Bit (list also includes Stretch, Loop, Pitch Env, Ring Mod, Sub Osc, Noise).","What is Pad FX Send Amount? <strong>Answer:</strong> How much of the Pad FX effect hits the selected pad (Manual §7.4) — different from FX Type."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["RN 1.2 Drum Sampler second page + X/Y","Manual Drum Sampler FX Type list","Ableton Note Manual §7.2.2 / §7.4 Pad FX vs Kit FX","Beatmaking: one shot of excitement, not every sound processed"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. One pad, one FX Type. Re-sequence still recognizable."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-4-4</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-4-5","title":"12.4.5 — Reverse tail as transition","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.4.5 — Reverse tail as transition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.4 — Lab: sample-chop sketch</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Reverse one chop or cymbal and place it as a one-shot that leads into a scene change."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Reverse</strong> arrives in RN <strong>1.0.12</strong>. It lives on the sample (Sample tab / Sample Options). Beatmaking names a reverse cymbal as a classic shot. Use a cymbal from the kit, a slice with a tail, or a recorded crash."},{"type":"prose","html":"Reverse on the sampler path is still subject to the FAQ speed rule if you also Transpose. Reverse first, keep Transpose near 0 if you need the tail to last."},{"type":"prose","html":"Put the reversed pad on its own clip in the last beat of a scene, or on a second scene that you launch into the re-sequence. Long-press clip → Duplicate / move. One shot, not a reversed loop for sixteen bars."},{"type":"prose","html":"If your version predates 1.0.12, Reverse is absent. {type:'gap'} Do not invent a workaround that the extracts do not describe. Use a short decaying shot instead and log the version."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Confirm version ≥ 1.0.12.","Select a tail-heavy pad (cymbal or long slice). Enable <strong>Reverse</strong>.","Capture a clip with a single hit near the end of a 1- or 2-bar loop, or paint one note in the editor.","Place that clip so it runs into the re-sequence scene (Scene 1 tail → Scene 2 chops, or the last beat of the chop scene).","Launch scenes. The reverse should point at the downbeat, not sit under the whole groove.","Write which sample you reversed."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Which release adds Reverse? <strong>Answer:</strong> Note 1.0.12 (RN).","Why is a reversed 16-bar loop a poor transition? <strong>Answer:</strong> Beatmaking shots are occasional; scenes handle form; 16 bars is the clip ceiling, not a riser length.","What if you transpose the reversed sample? <strong>Answer:</strong> Speed changes too on the sampler path (FAQ)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["RN 1.0.12 Reverse samples","Beatmaking: reverse cymbal shot","Note FAQ: transpose/speed on sampler path","Ableton Note Manual §4.3 Scenes; §9 samples"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. One reverse-tail clip used as a scene transition. Version logged."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-4-5</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"note-m-12-5-105","code":"12.5","title":"12.5","blurb":"12.5","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"note-l12-5-1","title":"12.5.1 — Map 8 macros on a sound-design-heavy preset","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.5.1 — Map 8 macros on a sound-design-heavy preset","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.5 — Lab: MIDI controller session</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Map all eight macros on one Track Preset to a class-compliant controller so each hardware knob moves a named Note macro."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Note accepts <strong>class-compliant</strong> USB or Bluetooth MIDI (no extra driver). USB-C on some iPads; others need a Lightning adapter. Power-hungry controllers need a <strong>powered hub</strong>. Enable the device toggle in Settings → Link &amp; MIDI → MIDI Input. Devices are remembered; switch the toggle off before unplug if you do not want auto-enable next time."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>MIDI Mapping:</strong> Settings (three dots) → MIDI Settings → <strong>Mapping</strong>. Tap a macro in Note, move a hardware control. Maximum <strong>eight</strong> macros. Pitch, length, velocity, aftertouch (including poly AT from 1.2.1) are recorded. <strong>Not</strong> MPE, pitch bend, or sustain."},{"type":"prose","html":"Pick a Drift or Wavetable preset with eight visible macros. Sound-design-heavy means you can hear each mapping. This is not a Live MIDI Map lesson and not a Launchkey course — only Note’s eight macros."},{"type":"prose","html":"If you have no controller, you cannot complete the hardware step. {type:'gap'} On-screen knobs still work; log the missing hardware and skip to documenting intended maps."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Connect the controller. Settings → MIDI Input → enable its toggle.","Open Mapping. Load a preset with up to eight macros.","Tap macro 1 in Note, move hardware knob 1. Repeat through eight or until macros run out.","Exit Mapping. Twist each hardware knob. Watch the Note macro move.","Play a pad so you hear the sound change.","Write hardware control → macro name for every slot."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["How many macros can you map? <strong>Answer:</strong> Eight (Manual §2.3.5; Note MIDI Input).","Which MIDI types are not supported? <strong>Answer:</strong> MPE, pitch bend, sustain (Note MIDI Input; FAQ pitch bend).","What does class-compliant mean here? <strong>Answer:</strong> No extra driver on iOS/iPadOS (Note MIDI Input)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §2.3 MIDI Input; §2.3.5 Mapping","Note MIDI Input KB","Note FAQ: MIDI controllers; no pitch bend","RN 1.0.15 MIDI mapping actions + 8 macros; 1.2.1 poly AT"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. Eight (or all visible) macros mapped. Chart started for 12.5.5."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-5-1</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-5-2","title":"12.5.2 — Map Capture + Start/Stop","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.5.2 — Map Capture + Start/Stop","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.5 — Lab: MIDI controller session</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Map Capture and Start/Stop (and optionally Clear Capture) so you can commit notes without hunting the on-screen buttons."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Mappable actions (Manual §2.3.5; RN 1.0.15): <strong>Capture</strong>, <strong>Clear Capture</strong>, <strong>Start/Stop</strong>, <strong>Quantize</strong>, <strong>Undo</strong>, <strong>Redo</strong>. In Mapping, tap the action’s <strong>Map</strong> button, then press a pad or button on the controller."},{"type":"prose","html":"Capture is how MIDI is recorded (FAQ). Mapping Capture does not change Fixed vs Free rules. Start/Stop is the same transport as the on-screen Play/Stop. Clear Capture is the <strong>X</strong> path for the uncommitted buffer — it does not delete an already stored clip."},{"type":"prose","html":"Leave one thumb on pads and one hand on the mapped buttons. That is the whole point of this lab. Do not map eight more things this step."},{"type":"prose","html":"Magic Keyboard (iPad, RN 1.2.1) has its own layout (space for Capture/transport). If you are on a Magic Keyboard instead of a MIDI controller, use that sourced layout rather than inventing keys."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Open Settings → MIDI Settings → <strong>Mapping</strong>.","Tap <strong>Map</strong> next to Capture. Press a spare controller button.","Map <strong>Start/Stop</strong> to another button.","Optional: map <strong>Clear Capture</strong>.","Exit Mapping. Press Start/Stop and confirm transport. Play pads, press Capture/Add as the UI requires, confirm notes store.","Write the two (or three) button names on the chart."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Which actions are sourced as mappable? <strong>Answer:</strong> Capture, Clear Capture, Start/Stop, Quantize, Undo, Redo.","Does mapping Capture bypass the Add / Create Clip rules? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. It triggers Capture; Fixed/Free/overdub rules still apply.","What is Clear Capture for? <strong>Answer:</strong> The uncommitted buffer (the X), not deleting stored clips."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §2.3.5 MIDI Mapping","Note MIDI Input: Mapping page","RN 1.0.15 MIDI mapping; 1.2.1 Magic Keyboard","Note FAQ: MIDI recording via Capture"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Six minutes. Capture + Start/Stop mapped and tested on an empty clip."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-5-2</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-5-3","title":"12.5.3 — Perform 2 minutes hands-on device only","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.5.3 — Perform 2 minutes hands-on device only","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.5 — Lab: MIDI controller session</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Play and Capture for two minutes using the hardware for notes, macros, Capture, and transport — not the glass."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The selected track is armed for the controller (Note MIDI Input). Change tracks from Session View if you need another instrument. Record the same way as pads: Fixed Length plus <strong>Add</strong>, or Free Length then Capture / Create Clip."},{"type":"prose","html":"Stay on wired headphones if you are playing time. Bluetooth MIDI controllers are supported; Bluetooth <strong>headphones</strong> still add 34–200 ms. Those are different Bluetooth uses."},{"type":"prose","html":"Two minutes. Beatmaking: intention first; do not evaluate mid-take. If you glance at the screen to confirm a dotted automation line, that is allowed — you still do not tap pads."},{"type":"prose","html":"No controller: you cannot meet the hardware rule. Log the gap and perform two minutes on pads instead, still without editing in the MIDI Editor during the take."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Load drums on one track and the mapped synth on another. Set tempo.","Start transport from the mapped Start/Stop.","For two minutes, play only the controller. Capture drum and synth passes with the mapped Capture.","Move macros from hardware during a playing clip if you want pending automation (commit in 12.5.4).","Stop from the hardware. Do not open the editor yet.","Write whether you touched the glass (yes/no) and which clips appeared."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Which track receives MIDI? <strong>Answer:</strong> The selected / open track, armed automatically (Note MIDI Input).","Why prefer wired headphones during this take? <strong>Answer:</strong> Headphone Bluetooth latency is 34–200 ms (Bluetooth KB).","Should you judge the take during the two minutes? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Beatmaking: create first, judge later."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note MIDI Input: arm selected track; Capture workflow","Ableton Note Manual §2.3; §8.1","Bluetooth Headphones and Latency in Note","Beatmaking: intention; delay-before-judge"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Two minutes on the clock. Hardware-only take. No editor."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-5-3</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-5-4","title":"12.5.4 — Capture automation from hardware knobs","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.5.4 — Capture automation from hardware knobs","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.5 — Lab: MIDI controller session</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Store automation that you performed on mapped macros so the clip plays the knob moves back."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Mapped macros are still Note macros. Transport running, move hardware knobs, dotted line in Clip Preview, tap <strong>Add</strong> (or mapped Capture if that is how your version commits automation — the sourced commit control is <strong>Add</strong>). Solid line + dots on those macros."},{"type":"prose","html":"You can move several macros and commit them in one Add. Return to Default stays greyed on automated macros until you Delete automation."},{"type":"prose","html":"This is not MPE and not pitch bend. Aftertouch may already be in the notes if the controller sent it (1.2.1 poly AT). That is note data, not knob automation."},{"type":"prose","html":"If no hardware, perform the same capture from on-screen macros and log the gap."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Launch a clip from the two-minute take. Transport running.","Move one or more mapped hardware knobs. Confirm dotted lines.","Tap <strong>Add</strong>. Confirm solid lines and dots.","Replay. Hands off. Knobs must move.","If a move is wrong, parameter menu → <strong>Delete</strong>, then recapture.","Add those parameter names to the mapping chart."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Does hardware mapping change the dotted/solid rule? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Same Capture automation rules (Manual §7.5).","Can you Return to Default on an automated macro? <strong>Answer:</strong> Not until you Delete the automation.","Is aftertouch the same as macro automation? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Aftertouch is MIDI input on notes; macros are mapped knobs."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §7.5 Automation; §2.3.5 Mapping","Capture in Note: Automation","Note MIDI Input: types of MIDI input vs mapping","RN 1.2.1 polyphonic aftertouch"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. At least one hardware-originated automation stored and verified."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-5-4</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-5-5","title":"12.5.5 — Document mapping chart","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.5.5 — Document mapping chart","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.5 — Lab: MIDI controller session</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Finish a one-page chart of every mapping in this Set so you can rebuild it after an update or a new controller."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Note remembers last-connected MIDI devices (RN 1.0.12). It does not, in these extracts, export a mapping file. The chart is your document. Module practice: mapping chart photo or notes."},{"type":"prose","html":"Include: Note version (Settings → Help), controller name, connection (USB / Bluetooth / powered hub), eight macro rows (hardware control → preset → macro name), action rows (Capture, Clear Capture, Start/Stop, Quantize, Undo, Redo), and whether poly aftertouch arrived."},{"type":"prose","html":"This is not Live MIDI Map. When the Set reaches Live, those Note macros are the surface you saved; Live has its own mapping (sister course)."},{"type":"prose","html":"If mappings vanished after unplug, you likely disabled the device toggle or opened a different Set. Re-enable the toggle; mappings are a Note MIDI Settings concern, not Cloud."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Open Mapping and photograph the screen if that is faster than typing.","Write the table: 8 macros + actions + version + controller + cable/BT.","Unplug and replug (or toggle Bluetooth). Confirm the device reappears (remembered devices).","Play one mapped knob. If it failed, remap and update the chart.","Store the chart with the Set name (artwork or Files note).","Close Mapping."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Do the extracts provide a mapping export? <strong>Answer:</strong> {type:'gap'} No. You keep a chart.","Are last-connected devices remembered? <strong>Answer:</strong> Yes (RN 1.0.12; Manual §2.3).","Which actions belong on the chart besides macros? <strong>Answer:</strong> Capture, Clear Capture, Start/Stop, Quantize, Undo, Redo."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §2.3.5; devices remembered","Note MIDI Input KB","RN 1.0.12 last-connected MIDI; 1.0.15 mapping","Module 12.5 practice: mapping chart photo/notes"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. Chart complete and stored next to the Set name."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-5-5</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"note-m-12-6-106","code":"12.6","title":"12.6","blurb":"12.6","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"note-l12-6-1","title":"12.6.1 — Enable Link both devices","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.6.1 — Enable Link both devices","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.6 — Lab: Link jam (if second device available)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Turn Ableton Link on in Note and on a second peer so Connected Peers shows at least one device."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Link keeps devices in time on a <strong>local network</strong> (wired or wireless). Peers sourced for Note: Push 3 standalone, Move, another iPhone/iPad with Note, other Link-enabled iOS apps, a computer with Live, other Link hardware (Using Link in Note). Same Wi-Fi or LAN."},{"type":"prose","html":"In Note: Sets view → App Settings → <strong>Link &amp; MIDI → Link</strong> → enable <strong>Ableton Link</strong>. Allow local network if iOS asks. <strong>Connected Peers</strong> shows “Connected to x peer” or “No peers connected.” Notifications can announce join/leave."},{"type":"prose","html":"This module is optional if you have no second device. Log that and read the failure modes lesson anyway."},{"type":"prose","html":"Link is tempo (and optional Start/Stop). It is not Cloud and not MIDI Network Session (that is a different Settings page)."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Put both devices on the same Wi-Fi or LAN.","Enable <strong>Ableton Link</strong> in Note. Allow local network.","Enable Link in the other app or Live.","Read <strong>Connected Peers</strong>. You want at least one peer.","Change tempo on one device. Confirm the other follows.","Write: peer name/type, network, peer count."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Where is the Note toggle? <strong>Answer:</strong> App Settings → Link &amp; MIDI → Link → Ableton Link.","What if Connected Peers stays at zero? <strong>Answer:</strong> Same Wi-Fi/LAN first (Using Link in Note). Then see 12.6.5.","Is Link the same as Cloud? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Link is local tempo sync; Cloud transfers Sets."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Using Link in Note KB","Ableton Note Manual §2.2.1 Link","Note FAQ: Link enable path","Note Compatibility: Link; Link Audio as of Live 12.4 and Note 2.0"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. Peer count ≥ 1 logged, or a written “no second device” skip."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-6-1</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-6-2","title":"12.6.2 — Sync Start/Stop on/off comparison","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.6.2 — Sync Start/Stop on/off comparison","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.6 — Lab: Link jam (if second device available)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Hear the difference between Link with Sync Start/Stop off (tempo only) and on (shared start/stop)."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"After Link is on, <strong>Sync Start/Stop</strong> can be enabled. Manual: it synchronizes playback position as well as tempo; start and stop on other devices start or stop Note at the corresponding point. Using Link in Note lists the same toggle."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Off:</strong> devices share tempo; you start Note when you want. <strong>On:</strong> a stop on Live or the other app stops Note too. RN notes persistence of this preference across launches (course Level 10). Use what you see in your version."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do both states on the same pair of devices. One variable. This is the comparison the module asks for."},{"type":"prose","html":"If you have no peer, you can still find the toggle and write what it claims to do."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Leave <strong>Sync Start/Stop</strong> off. Start Note. Start the peer. Confirm tempos match and starts do not.","Stop both. Enable <strong>Sync Start/Stop</strong> on Note (and on the peer if it has the option).","Start from the peer. Confirm Note starts. Stop from the peer. Confirm Note stops.","Disable the toggle. Repeat one start to feel tempo-only again.","Leave the state you want for the jam (12.6.3).","Write both results in one sentence each."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What does Sync Start/Stop add on top of Link? <strong>Answer:</strong> Shared start/stop (and, per Manual, playback position), not just tempo.","Does Link work with the toggle off? <strong>Answer:</strong> Yes. Tempo still syncs.","Where is the toggle? <strong>Answer:</strong> Link page, after Ableton Link is enabled (Manual §2.2.1; Using Link in Note)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §2.2.1 Sync Start/Stop","Using Link in Note KB","Note FAQ: Link","Course Level 10: persistence note (confirm in your version)"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. Two-state log: off vs on."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-6-2</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-6-3","title":"12.6.3 — Note provides drums; other app provides bass (or reverse)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.6.3 — Note provides drums; other app provides bass (or reverse)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.6 — Lab: Link jam (if second device available)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Split musical roles across Link peers so Note is not trying to be the whole band."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Link does not send Note’s MIDI clips to the other app. It aligns <strong>tempo</strong> (and Start/Stop if enabled). Each device still plays its own sound. That is why a role split works: Note holds the Drum Rack; the other app or Live holds bass (or the reverse)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Stay inside Note’s ceilings on the Note side (8 tracks, 8 scenes, 16-bar clips). Do not expect the other app’s arrangement to appear in Note. Do not use Cloud for this jam."},{"type":"prose","html":"Capture on Note as usual if you invent a new drum clip mid-jam. The other app is not documented here — if it fails, that is a third-party support issue (Using Link in Note)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Five-minute jam is enough. Beatmaking: intention (drums-only Note) and a limitation (no bass track on Note)."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["On Note, load only drums (mute or delete bass).","On the peer, load only bass (or whatever role you assigned).","Enable Link. Decide Sync Start/Stop.","Jam for five minutes. Change Note scenes; leave bass on the peer.","Optional swap: Note plays a bass preset; peer plays drums. Same five minutes is not required.","Write: who played drums, who played bass, whether tempo held."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Does Link copy Note clips onto the other app? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. It syncs tempo / optional start-stop only.","Why mute Note’s bass? <strong>Answer:</strong> The limitation is a role split; eight tracks are not an excuse to double the bass.","Who supports the other app if it will not join Link? <strong>Answer:</strong> That app’s developer (Using Link in Note)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Using Link in Note: what Link connects; third-party support","Ableton Note Manual §2.2.1","Beatmaking: limitation; intention","Note FAQ: Link"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Five-minute jam log: roles, Sync Start/Stop state, tempo lock yes/no."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-6-3</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-6-4","title":"12.6.4 — Link Audio to Live (2.x) optional","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.6.4 — Link Audio to Live (2.x) optional","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.6 — Lab: Link jam (if second device available)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"If you are on Note 2.0+ and Live 12.4+, stream Note’s audio to Live or Push from the Link menu — or log the version skip."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Link Audio</strong> is a Note <strong>2.0 / 2.0.1</strong> feature: new settings in the Link menu to live-stream Note’s audio to <strong>Live and Push</strong>. Compatibility extract: supported as of <strong>Live 12.4 and Note 2.0</strong>, <strong>sending audio only</strong>. FAQ: as of Note 2.0, audio can be sent to linked peers via Link Audio."},{"type":"prose","html":"This is optional. It is not a bounce and not Cloud. Use it when you want to hear Note inside Live <strong>during</strong> a jam without Export Audio. After the jam, a real transfer is still Cloud or .ablbundle plus Collect All and Save if you want the Set, not just the sound."},{"type":"prose","html":"{type:'gap'} The extracts do not give the full Live-side receive recipe beyond “Link Audio settings in the Link menu” and “stream to Live and Push.” Do not invent Live routing pages. Teach: enable the Audio option on Note’s Link page, confirm versions, listen in Live if it appears."},{"type":"prose","html":"Below 2.0: skip. Export Audio or bounce is the sourced alternative."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Settings → Help: confirm Note ≥ 2.0. Live: confirm ≥ 12.4 if you want Link Audio.","Enable Link. Open the Link Audio / <strong>Audio: Share Audio with Live</strong> option (Using Link in Note).","Enable it. Look at Live for incoming Link Audio (only as far as your Live version shows).","Play a Note clip. Confirm you hear Note in Live, or write that you cannot find the Live receive control.","Disable Link Audio. Confirm Note still plays locally.","Write versions + heard / not heard / skipped."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What versions introduce Link Audio for Note? <strong>Answer:</strong> Note 2.0 / 2.0.1; Live 12.4 (Compatibility; RN; FAQ).","Does Link Audio replace Cloud? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. It streams audio. Sets still transfer via Cloud or Share To….","Which direction is documented? <strong>Answer:</strong> Note sending audio to Live and Push (RN; Compatibility: sending audio only)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["RN 2.0.1 Link Audio","Note Compatibility: Link Audio as of Live 12.4 and Note 2.0, send only","Note FAQ: send audio via Link Audio as of 2.0","Using Link in Note: Audio: Share Audio with Live"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes or a documented skip. Versions written either way."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-6-4</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-6-5","title":"12.6.5 — Failure modes write-up","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.6.5 — Failure modes write-up","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.6 — Lab: Link jam (if second device available)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Write the Link failures you actually hit, mapped only to sourced checks."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Manual: Link generally works once enabled. If a peer fails, first check <strong>same Wi-Fi or LAN</strong>. Using Link in Note points at the Link FAQ, Live Link troubleshooting, and the other app’s developer. Do not invent firewall ports or a “Link reset” that the extracts do not name."},{"type":"prose","html":"Sourced confusion to rule out:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Link vs MIDI Network Session</strong> — different Settings pages. Network Session is MIDI from a Mac, not tempo Link.","<strong>Link vs Cloud</strong> — Cloud needs internet + account; Link needs local network.","<strong>Link Audio missing</strong> — Note &lt; 2.0 or Live &lt; 12.4.","<strong>Bluetooth headphones</strong> — latency is not a Link failure.","<strong>Sync Start/Stop surprise stop</strong> — toggle is on.","<strong>No second device</strong> — not a failure; skip the jam."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"Write what you saw (Connected Peers text, notifications) and which check fixed it — or that it did not."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["List every attempt from 12.6.1–12.6.4: peer type, result.","For each failure, run: same network → Link toggle both sides → Sync Start/Stop state → version for Link Audio.","Note any iOS local-network permission deny.","Do not change Cloud settings as a Link fix.","Write a 6–10 line failure card.","Keep it with the jam log."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["First check when no peers appear? <strong>Answer:</strong> Same Wi-Fi/LAN (Using Link in Note).","Is a missing Link Audio control a network failure? <strong>Answer:</strong> Not if Note is pre-2.0 or Live is pre-12.4.","Does unpairing Bluetooth headphones fix Link? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. That is a latency path (Bluetooth KB), not Link."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Using Link in Note; Manual §2.2.1","Note Compatibility: Link Audio versions","Bluetooth Headphones and Latency in Note","Note FAQ: Link vs Cloud vs MIDI"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One failure card, even if the only line is “no second device.”"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-6-5</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"note-m-12-7-107","code":"12.7","title":"12.7","blurb":"12.7","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"note-l12-7-1","title":"12.7.1 — After Collect All and Save: freeze risky third-party later","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.7.1 — After Collect All and Save: freeze risky third-party later","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.7 — Live expansion recipes (hand-off only)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Open the Note Set in Live, run Collect All and Save first, and treat freeze/third-party work as a later Live job."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"This module is a hand-off pointer, not a Live course. After Cloud or .ablbundle, open the Set in <strong>Live 11.2.5+</strong>. <strong>File → Collect All and Save</strong> copies referenced samples into the Live Project so they survive if you remove the Note Set from Cloud (Manual §10.1; FAQ; Troubleshooting Problems with Note Files)."},{"type":"prose","html":"{type:'gap'} Note extracts do not document Live’s Freeze command or third-party plugin freeze behavior. Do not invent freeze steps here. The sourced order is: Collect All and Save <strong>immediately</strong>, then any Live expansion (sister Ableton Live 12 course). Third-party plugins do not exist in Note (no AUv3). They appear only after you add them in Live — after the Note material is collected."},{"type":"prose","html":"If samples go missing, the KB path is: original Note Set removed from Cloud, or User Library on a disconnected drive. Re-add the Set to Cloud, reconnect the drive, then Collect All and Save again."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Upload via Cloud or open the .ablbundle in Live 11.2.5+.","Verify tracks, samples, and effects you had in Note.","<strong>Collect All and Save</strong> now — before adding plugins, before deleting Cloud slots.","Save a Live-side name that includes “Note origin.”","Write: “Freeze / third-party = later, Live course. Not a Note operation.”","Do not try to send the Live Set back to Note."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What is the first Live command after opening a Note Set? <strong>Answer:</strong> Collect All and Save.","Why before deleting the Cloud slot? <strong>Answer:</strong> Cloud samples can go missing in Live if the Note Set is removed first (Troubleshooting Problems with Note Files).","Is Freeze a Note feature? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. {type:'gap'} Live-only; sister course."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §10.1 Collect All and Save; one-way transfer","Note FAQ: Collect All and Save; no AUv3; no Live→Note","Troubleshooting Problems with Note Files","Using Note Presets in Live"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One Live Set collected and saved. No plugins added in this lesson."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-7-1</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-7-2","title":"12.7.2 — Promote Note Drum Rack hits in Live","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.7.2 — Promote Note Drum Rack hits in Live","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.7 — Live expansion recipes (hand-off only)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"In Live’s Cloud folder, find the Note Drum Rack samples and know they are already in the Set after Collect All and Save."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"When a Note Set lands in Live’s browser <strong>Cloud</strong> folder, you get a Project-like folder: samples, recordings, the <strong>.abl</strong> file, and the <strong>.ablbundle</strong>. You can expand the Set to individual tracks or double-click the bundle (Manual §10.1). Drum hits you recorded in Note are those files."},{"type":"prose","html":"“Promote” here means: locate the sample, keep it collected, and — if you want the sound in other Live Sets — save the device as a User Library preset (Using Note Presets in Live: open Device View, <strong>Save Preset</strong>). It does not mean inventing a Live Drum Rack rebuild recipe."},{"type":"prose","html":"Note Drum Rack = 16 pads, each a Drum Sampler + pad FX send + kit FX. In Live those devices open as themselves (or as the Note surface). Deeper Live drum editing is the Drums / Live sister courses."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not drag samples out and delete the only copy before Collect All and Save."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["In Live’s browser, open <strong>Cloud</strong> (or the folder from an .ablbundle).","Expand the Note Set. Find <strong>Samples</strong> / <strong>Recordings</strong> and the drum track.","Confirm the hits play in the opened Live Set.","If Collect All and Save is not done, do it now.","Optional: Save Preset on the Drum Rack for User Library.","Write the folder path you used (Cloud vs local Project after collect)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Where do Note samples appear in Live before collect? <strong>Answer:</strong> Inside the Cloud Set folder (and User Library paths if that is how Live stored them). After collect, also in the Live Project.","How do you keep a Note drum preset for other Live Sets? <strong>Answer:</strong> Save Preset to User Library (Using Note Presets in Live).","Should you delete the Note Cloud Set first? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Collect All and Save first."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §10.1 Cloud folder contents","Using Note Presets in Live","Troubleshooting Problems with Note Files (missing samples)"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. Locate drum samples in Live. Collect if needed. Optional Save Preset."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-7-2</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-7-3","title":"12.7.3 — Replace mobile Drift macros with deeper Live routing (pointer)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.7.3 — Replace mobile Drift macros with deeper Live routing (pointer)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.7 — Live expansion recipes (hand-off only)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Know what the Note Drift (or Wavetable) surface becomes in Live, then stop before this course teaches Live routing."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Note Drift shows a <strong>preset-specific</strong> subset of parameters. Full Drift pages exist on Note only if the manual’s purchase/restore path is available on your storefront (FAQ IAP conflict → gap). In Live, a Note preset is saved with <strong>Save Preset</strong>; you then open the Live device."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Wavetable</strong> from Note in Lite/Intro/Standard is a <strong>locked rack</strong>: Note macros only. Suite (or the Pack) unlocks the full device (Using Note Presets in Live). Do not tell Standard users to “open Osc 2” if they see a locked rack."},{"type":"prose","html":"{type:'gap'} Deeper Live routing (sends, racks, parallel chains) is not in the Note extracts. Pointer only: sister <strong>Ableton Live 12</strong> and <strong>Sound Design</strong> courses. The honest hand-off is: keep the Note macros sounding, Collect All and Save, then expand in Live if your edition allows."},{"type":"prose","html":"Replacing macros is optional. Many sketches do not need it."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["In Live, double-click the Drift or Wavetable track header.","Write what you see: Note-style macros, full Drift, or locked Wavetable rack.","Save Preset to User Library if you want it again.","Do <strong>not</strong> build a new Live rack in this lesson.","Write one sentence: “Next Live job = ____” or “macros are enough.”","Close Device View."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What do Standard users get for Note Wavetable? <strong>Answer:</strong> A locked rack; Note-visible controls only (Using Note Presets in Live).","Are Note Drift knobs the entire Drift device? <strong>Answer:</strong> Not necessarily. Note shows a subset per preset (Manual §7.2.1).","Why is this a pointer lesson? <strong>Answer:</strong> Live routing is a sister course; extracts stop at Save Preset and locked-rack behavior."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Using Note Presets in Live (locked Wavetable)","Ableton Note Manual §7.2.1 Drift subset; purchase/restore","Note FAQ: IAP line; presets in Live","Course syllabus 12.7: Live hand-off only"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Six minutes. One Device View observation written. No new Live routing."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-7-3</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-7-4","title":"12.7.4 — Arrangement View is a Live job (sister course)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.7.4 — Arrangement View is a Live job (sister course)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.7 — Live expansion recipes (hand-off only)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"State why the sketch stays in Session on Note and why linear arrangement happens only in Live."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Note’s only musical grid is <strong>Session View</strong>: tracks vertical, scenes horizontal. There is no Arrangement View (Ableton Note.md; Manual Session chapter). Scenes (max 8) and clip length (max 16 bars) are how you imply form. Export Audio renders scenes <strong>top to bottom</strong>."},{"type":"prose","html":"Live has Session <strong>and</strong> Arrangement. Once the Note Set is a Live Set, recording or arranging scenes onto a timeline is a <strong>Live</strong> job (Ableton Live 12 sister course). You cannot design that timeline in Note and send it back."},{"type":"prose","html":"This is a design limit, not a missing checkbox. Beatmaking already told you to avoid the endless loop by making sections — those sections are scenes until Live."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not pretend Note 2.x audio tracks are Arrangement View. They are warped audio <strong>clips</strong> in Session."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["In Note, count your scenes and the longest clip. Write both numbers.","Export Audio once if you need a linear listen of scene order.","In Live, notice Session clips arrived; do not record Arrangement in this lesson.","Write: “Arrangement = Live course. Note form = scenes.”","Keep Collect All and Save already done.","Return to Note only to sketch, not to “fix the arrangement.”"],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Does Note have Arrangement View? <strong>Answer:</strong> No.","How does Export Audio linearize the Set? <strong>Answer:</strong> Scenes top to bottom; longest clip per scene sets length (Manual §10.2).","Can you arrange in Live and reopen that Live Set in Note? <strong>Answer:</strong> No (FAQ; Manual §10.1)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §4 Session View; §10.1–10.2","Ableton Note.md: Session only; not mobile Live","Note FAQ: 8 scenes; 16-bar clips; no Live→Note","Beatmaking: sections vs endless loop","Syllabus sister-course table"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Six minutes. Written sentence: scene count + “Arrangement is Live.”"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-7-4</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-7-5","title":"12.7.5 — Keep a “Note origin” locator/comment habit in Live","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.7.5 — Keep a “Note origin” locator/comment habit in Live","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.7 — Live expansion recipes (hand-off only)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Leave a written Note-origin mark on the Live Set so you still know version, Cloud slot, and clip sources after months."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"{type:'gap'} Note extracts do not document Live locators or clip comments. This lesson is a <strong>student habit</strong>, not a Note control. After Collect All and Save, record on paper or in a Live text/comment field <strong>you already know how to use</strong> from the Live course: Set name, Note version (Settings → Help), date, Cloud vs .ablbundle, scene map, sample paths."},{"type":"prose","html":"Why it matters: Cloud holds <strong>8</strong> Sets and is not backup. You will rotate slots. Live Projects remain after the Note Cloud copy is gone — if you collected. The mark stops you from hunting which phone Set made this Project."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not invent a required locator color or a Note feature that writes into Live. Name the Live Set clearly (the same discipline as Note’s Rename)."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Confirm Collect All and Save is done.","Write a 5-line origin card: Note version, Set name, transfer path, scene count, one sample source.","Store that card in the Live Project folder (text file) or a comment you already use in Live.","Rename the Live Set if the name is still “Set 12.”","Do not delete the Note local copy until Share To… backup exists.","Photograph the card into your course notes."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Is “Note origin locator” a button in Note? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. {type:'gap'} It is a Live-side / notes habit.","Why write the Note version? <strong>Answer:</strong> Features are version-gated (audio tracks, Slice, Link Audio).","Does Cloud keep this card? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Cloud is transfer, not archive (FAQ)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ: Cloud not backup; 8 Sets; version in Settings → Help","Ableton Note Manual §10.1 Collect All and Save","Sharing Note Sets: Share To… backup","Syllabus 12.7: habit, not Live dump"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Six minutes. Origin card stored next to the Live Project."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-7-5</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-7-6","title":"12.7.6 — Save Note-origin presets to User Library taxonomy","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.7.6 — Save Note-origin presets to User Library taxonomy","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.7 — Live expansion recipes (hand-off only)</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Save the Note devices you still want in Live’s User Library, and keep names that say they came from Note."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Using Note Presets in Live: share via Cloud or Share To…, open the Set, double-click a track header, <strong>Save Preset</strong>. The preset appears in Live’s Browser → <strong>User Library</strong>. Wavetable from Note stays locked in Lite/Intro/Standard."},{"type":"prose","html":"{type:'gap'} The KB does not prescribe a folder taxonomy beyond User Library. Do not invent official Ableton folders named “Note Origin.” You may name the preset <code>Note - &lt;Set&gt; - &lt;role&gt;</code> so you can find it. That is your naming, not a product path."},{"type":"prose","html":"On Note itself, user presets already save to Note’s <strong>User Library</strong> by instrument category (Manual §7.1.2). Those do not automatically become Live presets until you Save Preset in Live."},{"type":"prose","html":"Only specifically created presets can go <strong>Live → Note</strong> (FAQ; Presets on Move &amp; Note). Do not expect every Live rack to travel back."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["In Live, open the handed-off Set.","Save Preset on the drum rack, the bass, and one melodic device you still like.","Prefix names with <code>Note</code>.","Browse User Library and confirm the three files.","Write whether Wavetable is locked (edition).","Do not export a Live preset back to Note unless you are on the Move/Note special path (Appendix A.5)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["How does a Note sound become a Live User Library preset? <strong>Answer:</strong> Open the Note Set in Live → Save Preset (Using Note Presets in Live).","Can any Live preset be sent to Note? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Only specifically created presets (FAQ).","Is there an official “Note Origin” folder in the extracts? <strong>Answer:</strong> {type:'gap'} No. User Library + your names."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Using Note Presets in Live","Note FAQ: presets Note↔Live; Move &amp; Note pointer","Ableton Note Manual §7.1.2 User Presets (Note side)","Appendix A.5 / syllabus 11.2.17 pointer"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. At least one Note-origin preset saved in Live User Library with a clear name."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-7-6</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"note-m-12-8-108","code":"12.8","title":"12.8","blurb":"12.8","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"note-l12-8-1","title":"12.8.1 — Max 8 tracks: force layering choices","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.8.1 — Max 8 tracks: force layering choices","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.8 — Limits-as-creativity drills</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Fill eight tracks on purpose, then delete or merge until every remaining track has a named job."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"FAQ and Manual: a Note Set has a <strong>maximum of 8 tracks</strong>. Swipe left → <strong>Add Track</strong>. Long-press to reorder, duplicate, or delete. Note 2.x add buttons: <strong>Beat, Synth, Audio</strong> (RN 2.0.1). You cannot add a ninth track."},{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking limitations (“I’m going to write a beat with no bass line”) are the pedagogy. Eight tracks is the product’s limitation. Layering choices: drums, bass, harmony, lead, shot, bed — if you also want Link-role leftovers, something must go."},{"type":"prose","html":"Resample (long-press mic) can bounce a stack onto one Sampler pad, freeing tracks. That is a sourced Note operation, not a secret mixer. Do not pretend a Track Preset’s two FX slots are extra tracks."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Open a lab Set or <strong>+ New</strong>. Add tracks until <strong>Add Track</strong> stops (8).","Give each track a role in the name or on paper (drums, bass, chords, lead, hats, shot, bed, spare).","If two tracks do the same job, long-press <strong>Delete</strong> one, or resample them onto one pad and delete the sources.","Play the Set. Every audible part should map to one remaining track.","Write the eight-or-fewer role list.","Do not add Live tracks in this lesson."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What is the track ceiling? <strong>Answer:</strong> Eight (FAQ; Manual §4.1).","How do you add a track? <strong>Answer:</strong> Swipe left, tap Add Track (2.x: Beat / Synth / Audio).","How can resample help the ceiling? <strong>Answer:</strong> Long-press mic → Resample Output records Note’s output onto one pad (Manual §9.1)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ: max 8 tracks","Ableton Note Manual §4.1 Tracks; §9.1 Resample","RN 2.0.1 Beat / Synth / Audio add buttons","Beatmaking: limitation as focus"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. Hit the 8-track wall, then cut back to named roles."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-8-1</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-8-2","title":"12.8.2 — Max 8 scenes: force arrangement economy","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.8.2 — Max 8 scenes: force arrangement economy","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.8 — Limits-as-creativity drills</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Use all eight scene slots once, then keep only the rows that change density or role."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Eight scenes</strong> is the ceiling (FAQ; Manual §4.3). Long-press a scene number to duplicate, rearrange, or delete. Show/Hide scene numbers to launch rows."},{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking sections: hook, verse, intro/outro. That is three to five rows for most sketches. Eight is a hard max, not a quota. Economy means Scene 7 should not be Scene 1 again."},{"type":"prose","html":"Export Audio will play whatever rows exist, top to bottom — empty or duplicate rows become dead air or repeats in the bounce. Delete unused rows before export."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Show scene numbers. Duplicate Scene 1 until you have 8 rows (or add clips down the grid).","Launch 1 through 8. Mark which rows are identical.","Delete or rewrite duplicates so each remaining scene changes hats, shot, or lead.","Reorder intro → verse → hook if that is your story.","Count remaining scenes. Write the job of each.","Optional: Export Audio and confirm the bounce follows that order."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["How many scenes can a Set have? <strong>Answer:</strong> Eight.","How do you launch a whole row? <strong>Answer:</strong> Tap the scene number.","Why delete empty scenes before export? <strong>Answer:</strong> Export is scenes top to bottom; empty rows still consume the bounce if they have a longest clip — empty rows with no clips contribute nothing, but duplicate full rows repeat."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ: 8 scenes","Ableton Note Manual §4.3 Scenes; §10.2 Export order","Beatmaking: chorus, verse, intro/outro"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. Eight rows created, then culled to distinct sections. List kept."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-8-2</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-8-3","title":"12.8.3 — Max 16 bars: force sections via scenes not endless clips","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.8.3 — Max 16 bars: force sections via scenes not endless clips","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.8 — Limits-as-creativity drills</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Refuse to fake a song by stretching one clip to 16 bars; put sections on scenes instead."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Clips are <strong>maximum 16 bars</strong> (FAQ; RN 1.0.15 raised length and allowed uneven lengths). Fixed Length plus icon offers 1, 2, 4, 8, or 16. Free Length stopped caps at <strong>8 bars</strong> before Capture. Transport running + Create Clip follows the shortest existing clip (at least that long)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Sixteen bars is still a loop. Beatmaking: an amazing loop that goes nowhere is a starting point, not a song. Sections are <strong>scenes</strong>. Duplicate a 2-bar clip into Scene 2 and change it; do not grow Scene 1’s clip to 16 just because you can."},{"type":"prose","html":"MIDI Editor loop brace: Duplicate / Crop / Zoom. Crop a sloppy Free Length capture instead of keeping dead bars."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Capture a 2-bar idea (drums or chords).","Try to add bars past 16 — the UI will not allow it. Write that fact.","Duplicate the clip to Scene 2. Change one part (hats, shot, chord).","Crop any clip that has empty bars you do not use.","Launch Scene 1 then Scene 2. That is the section change.","Write: longest clip length + scene count."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What is the clip length ceiling? <strong>Answer:</strong> 16 bars (FAQ; RN 1.0.15).","How long can a stopped Free Length performance be before Capture? <strong>Answer:</strong> Up to 8 bars (Manual §8.1.2).","Why are scenes the section tool? <strong>Answer:</strong> Note has no Arrangement View; Beatmaking sections map to rows."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ: max clip length 16 bars","RN 1.0.15 16-bar clips; uneven lengths","Ableton Note Manual §8.1.1–8.1.2; §8.2.4 loop brace","Beatmaking: loop vs sections"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. One 2-bar clip, one scene change, no 16-bar “fake song.”"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-8-3</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-8-4","title":"12.8.4 — 8 Cloud slots: ruthless curation","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.8.4 — 8 Cloud slots: ruthless curation","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.8 — Limits-as-creativity drills</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Treat the eight Cloud slots as a transfer queue you rotate, not as a disc."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Cloud holds <strong>8 Sets</strong> (FAQ; RN <strong>1.2</strong> raised the cap from 5). Same Ableton account email as the Live license. Enable: Settings toggle, library banner, or Set Options → Upload. Offline uploads wait for a connection. Multi-device: same account sees the same Cloud Sets, including Move/Push Sets already stored."},{"type":"prose","html":"Cloud is <strong>not backup</strong>. Local copies stay in Files → On My iPhone/iPad → Ableton Note → <strong>Projects</strong>. Before you evict a Cloud Set, <strong>Share To…</strong> an .ablbundle or confirm Live already <strong>Collect All and Save</strong>’d it."},{"type":"prose","html":"Ruthless: only Sets that must appear in Live or on another device this week earn a slot. Hero Sets later (Level 13.5) get long-term slots; everything else is Local + Files."},{"type":"prose","html":"100 MB sample warning can stall a fat Set — another reason to curate."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Count Cloud Sets in the library. Write n/8.","For each Cloud Set, mark: needed in Live this week / already collected / evict.","Share To… Files any evict candidate that is not in Live.","Remove evictions from Cloud (library/Cloud controls in your version).","Upload the one Set this drill needs.","Confirm the local Project still exists."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["How many Cloud Sets? <strong>Answer:</strong> Eight (was five before Note 1.2).","If you delete a Set from the device, is the Cloud copy a backup of last month? <strong>Answer:</strong> Cloud is sync/transfer, not an archive (FAQ). Local Projects are the files.","What must you do in Live before evicting a Cloud Set you opened there? <strong>Answer:</strong> Collect All and Save."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ: 8 Sets; not backup; same account","RN 1.2 Cloud 8 (was 5)","Ableton Note Manual §2.1; §10.1","Sharing Note Sets; Troubleshooting missing Cloud files"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. Cloud count written, one eviction archived, one upload."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-8-4</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-8-5","title":"12.8.5 — No MIDI file I/O: Capture is the highway","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.8.5 — No MIDI file I/O: Capture is the highway","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.8 — Limits-as-creativity drills</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Prove you can get notes into and out of Note without a MIDI file, because MIDI import/export does not exist."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"FAQ: <strong>MIDI clips cannot be imported into or exported from Note.</strong> No <code>.mid</code> highway. Notes enter by <strong>Capture</strong> (pads, class-compliant MIDI, other iOS apps via MIDI Input, or Mac Network Session). Notes leave as part of a <strong>Note Set</strong> (Cloud or .ablbundle) into Live, or as <strong>Export Audio</strong>."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not hunt a MIDI export in Share To…. Share To… makes an <strong>.ablbundle</strong>, not a Standard MIDI File."},{"type":"prose","html":"Limitation as pedagogy: if a collaborator wants a MIDI file, they open the bundle or Cloud Set in Live (11.2.5+) and export MIDI <strong>there</strong> (Live course). In Note, play it again or send the Set."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Open Share To… on a Set. Confirm the file is <code>.ablbundle</code>, not <code>.mid</code>.","Capture a 1-bar phrase from pads or a controller.","Export Audio of a scene so you have an audio takeaway.","Write the inbound path you used (pads / USB / Bluetooth / app / network).","Write the outbound path (Cloud / bundle / WAV / M4A).","Do not search for MIDI export again."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Can you import a MIDI file into Note? <strong>Answer:</strong> No (FAQ).","What file does Share To… create? <strong>Answer:</strong> .ablbundle (Set + samples + metadata).","How do notes get in? <strong>Answer:</strong> Capture from pads or MIDI input (FAQ; Note MIDI Input)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ: no MIDI import/export; Capture; Share To…","Sharing Note Sets","Note MIDI Input","Ableton Note Manual §8.1 Capture; §10 export/transfer"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. One Capture in, one audio or bundle out. No .mid file."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-8-5</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-8-6","title":"12.8.6 — No Live→Note: finish path is one-way by design","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.8.6 — No Live→Note: finish path is one-way by design","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.8 — Limits-as-creativity drills</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"State the one-way rule from memory and plan finishing work so it never needs to return to Note."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"FAQ and Manual: <strong>Live Sets cannot be opened in Note.</strong> Cloud is Note → Live / other Note installs / Move / Push, not back. Once you import a Note Set into Live and save it as a Live Set, that modified version cannot open in Note."},{"type":"prose","html":"This is compatibility (Windows Live, no AUv3 in Note) and product intent (Note is a sketchbook). It is not a bug you ticket every week."},{"type":"prose","html":"Finish path: sketch in Note → Cloud or .ablbundle → Live 11.2.5+ → Collect All and Save → Arrangement and mix in Live. If you still need mobile work, <strong>duplicate the Note Set before</strong> the Live-only edits, and keep sketching on the Note copy. Those two files will diverge."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Write the one-way sentence without looking: “Live Sets cannot open in Note.”","On a handed-off idea, list three Live-only jobs (Arrangement, plugins, extra tracks).","Duplicate the Note Set (Set Options → Duplicate) if you still want a mobile sketch.","Confirm Cloud will not pull the Live Project back.","Put the Live job list on the origin card (12.7.5).","Do not search Settings for “download from Live.”"],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Can Cloud send a Live Set to Note? <strong>Answer:</strong> No (FAQ).","What still syncs to another iPhone? <strong>Answer:</strong> Note Sets on the same Ableton Cloud account — not Live Projects.","How do you keep a mobile version after hand-off? <strong>Answer:</strong> Duplicate/keep the Note Set locally; it will not include later Live edits."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ: no Live→Note; Cloud purpose","Ableton Note Manual §10.1 one-way","Note Compatibility: Live Sets cannot open in Note","Ableton Note.md: sketchbook, not mobile Live"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Six minutes. One-way sentence + Live-only job list + Note duplicate if needed."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-8-6</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-8-7","title":"12.8.7 — Write a “limits I used” paragraph for capstone","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.8.7 — Write a “limits I used” paragraph for capstone","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.8 — Limits-as-creativity drills</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Write one paragraph that names the hard limits you used on purpose, for Gate J process notes."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Gate J asks for process notes (verbs: setup, capture, edit, sample, automate, send) and whether limits were used creatively (11.4.7). This paragraph is that evidence."},{"type":"prose","html":"Use only sourced limits: <strong>8 tracks</strong>, <strong>8 scenes</strong>, <strong>16-bar clips</strong>, <strong>8 Cloud Sets</strong>, <strong>no MIDI I/O</strong>, <strong>no Live→Note</strong>, <strong>no AUv3</strong>, <strong>no pitch bend</strong>, <strong>no Android</strong>, <strong>two FX per track</strong>, <strong>Capture as the record path</strong>, sampler <strong>transpose=speed</strong> (vs 2.x audio warp). Plus Beatmaking limits you chose (no bass, two notes, time box)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not invent a limit Note does not have. Do not apologize for Session View."},{"type":"prose","html":"Practice for 12.8: one Set that intentionally hits <strong>three</strong> hard limits. Name those three in the paragraph."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Pick one lab Set. List every ceiling it actually touches.","Circle three you used as creative rules.","Write 120–180 words: what you refused, what you captured instead, what must go to Live.","Add Note version and working title.","Store the paragraph with the Set (Files note or paper).","Re-read once after a delay; keep it if it is still true."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Name four sourced product ceilings. <strong>Answer:</strong> 8 tracks, 8 scenes, 16-bar clips, 8 Cloud Sets (plus no MIDI I/O, one-way Cloud).","Is “no Arrangement View” a bug? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. It is the Session-only design (Ableton Note.md; Manual).","Why does Gate J want this paragraph? <strong>Answer:</strong> Process notes and creative use of limits (syllabus 11.4 / 11.4.7)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ: limits list","Ableton Note Manual: Session, Cloud, Capture","Beatmaking: limitation; delay-before-judge","Syllabus Gate J deliverables; 12.8 practice"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One paragraph stored. Three limits named."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-8-7</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"note-m-12-9-109","code":"12.9","title":"12.9","blurb":"12.9","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"note-l12-9-1","title":"12.9.1 — Show Touches on","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.9.1 — Show Touches on","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.9 — Teaching &amp; documentation labs</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Turn Show Touches on so every tap shows a white circle before you record a tutorial."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Show Touches</strong> lives in App Settings → <strong>Preferences → Other</strong>. Enabling it adds a small <strong>white circle</strong> that follows your gestures (Manual §2.4.5.1). RN <strong>1.0.12</strong> moved touch visualization to Preferences. The screen-recording KB tells you to enable Show Touches so taps are visible in a video."},{"type":"prose","html":"This is a teaching tool, not a musical effect. High Contrast is a different Preferences → Themes control (Appendix B). Direct-touch on pads/waveforms (RN 1.0.6) is also different — that is how you hit the control, not the white circle."},{"type":"prose","html":"Leave Show Touches on for 12.9.2. Turn it off afterward if the circle distracts you while playing."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["From the Set Library, tap the <strong>three dots</strong> (App Settings).","Open <strong>Preferences</strong>. Enable <strong>Show Touches</strong>.","Open a Set. Tap pads, sliders, and Set Settings. Confirm the white circle.","Disable it once, confirm the circle vanishes, then enable it again.","Leave it on for the next lesson.","Write the menu path from memory."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What does Show Touches draw? <strong>Answer:</strong> A small white circle that follows your gestures (Manual §2.4.5.1).","Where is the toggle? <strong>Answer:</strong> App Settings → Preferences (Other). RN 1.0.12 moved it there.","Is Show Touches the same as High Contrast? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. High Contrast is the AAA theme."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §2.4.5.1 Show Touches","RN 1.0.12 touch visualization moved to Preferences","How to Create a Screen Recording in Note"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Five minutes. Toggle on, prove the circle, leave it on."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-9-1</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-9-2","title":"12.9.2 — Screen record a Capture→Edit→Scene workflow","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.9.2 — Screen record a Capture→Edit→Scene workflow","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.9 — Teaching &amp; documentation labs</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Record a 60–90 second iOS screen video of Capture, a MIDI Editor fix, and a scene launch, with Show Touches visible."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"How to Create a Screen Recording in Note: add <strong>Screen Recording</strong> to iOS Control Center (Apple’s Record the screen instructions). Enable access within apps if iOS asks. Enable <strong>Show Touches</strong> in Note. Open Control Center <strong>while Note is in the foreground</strong> and start recording. Note keeps the screen awake in the foreground (RN 1.0.15), which helps."},{"type":"prose","html":"Ableton asks for screen recordings when a crash is reproducible or you want to share a performance. This lab is the teaching version of that path."},{"type":"prose","html":"Workflow to show: Fixed or Free <strong>Capture</strong> → tap Clip Preview → one edit (delete or length) → back to Session → launch a <strong>scene number</strong>. Sixty to ninety seconds. Do not narrate a full house mix."},{"type":"prose","html":"Save the video to Photos. It is process evidence for Gate J notes."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Confirm <strong>Show Touches</strong> is on.","Add Screen Recording to Control Center if it is missing (iOS Settings).","Open the practice Set. Start Control Center recording.","Capture a short clip. Open the editor. Change one note. Return. Launch a scene.","Stop recording from Control Center. Watch the video; taps must be visible.","Write the video filename and duration."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Why enable Show Touches before recording? <strong>Answer:</strong> So taps are visible in the video (Screen Recording KB).","Where do you start the recording? <strong>Answer:</strong> iOS Control Center, after adding Screen Recording there.","How long should this lab’s video be? <strong>Answer:</strong> About 60–90 seconds (module practice)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["How to Create a Screen Recording in Note","Ableton Note Manual §2.4.5.1; §8.1; §8.2; §4.3","RN 1.0.15 screen stays awake in foreground","Module 12.9 practice: 60–90 second recording"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Fifteen minutes including iOS setup. One 60–90 second video stored."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-9-2</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-9-3","title":"12.9.3 — High Contrast for outdoor visibility test","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.9.3 — High Contrast for outdoor visibility test","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.9 — Teaching &amp; documentation labs</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Switch to the High Contrast (AAA) theme and confirm you can still hit Capture, scenes, and mixer outdoors or in glare."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Preferences → <strong>Themes</strong>: <strong>Dark</strong> or <strong>High Contrast</strong>. RN <strong>1.0.12</strong> adds the <strong>AAA High Contrast</strong> theme. That is an accessibility contrast rating, not a different Session engine."},{"type":"prose","html":"Use it when sunlight washes Dark UI. This lab is a visibility test: Set Settings, Add Clip, Capture/Add, scene numbers, mixer <strong>M</strong>/<strong>S</strong>. If a control vanishes in glare, High Contrast is the sourced fix — not a third-party overlay."},{"type":"prose","html":"VoiceOver is separate (Appendix B). Show Touches can stay on. Direct-touch on pads/waveforms (1.0.6) still applies."},{"type":"prose","html":"Switch back to Dark if you prefer it indoors."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["App Settings → Preferences → Themes → <strong>High Contrast</strong>.","Open a Set in a bright place or facing a window.","Set tempo, Capture one note, launch a scene, and toggle mixer mute.","Switch to <strong>Dark</strong>. Repeat the same four actions.","Write which theme kept labels readable.","Leave the theme you will teach with."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Which release adds High Contrast? <strong>Answer:</strong> Note 1.0.12 (AAA).","Where is the control? <strong>Answer:</strong> App Settings → Preferences → Themes.","Does High Contrast add tracks or scenes? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. It is a UI theme."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §2.4.1 Themes","RN 1.0.12 AAA High Contrast","Appendix B.1 (same control, teaching angle here)"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Eight minutes. Outdoor or window A/B. Theme choice written."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-9-3</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-9-4","title":"12.9.4 — Process notes template (verbs checklist)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.9.4 — Process notes template (verbs checklist)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.9 — Teaching &amp; documentation labs</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Fill a one-page process template using Gate J’s verbs so every later sketch can reuse the same card."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Gate J process notes use the verbs <strong>setup, capture, edit, sample, automate, send</strong>. Beatmaking supplies the rest: working title, prompt, limitation, intention, delay, memorable yes/no."},{"type":"prose","html":"Template (copy this; do not invent product facts):"},{"type":"list","items":["Note version (Settings → Help)","Working title / prompt / limitation / intention","Tempo (how set: slider / tap / first Capture) — no genre BPM table","Key &amp; Scale (In Key on/off, root, scale)","Setup: tracks and presets","Capture: Fixed vs Free vs overdub, clip lengths","Edit: editor ops or Quantize","Sample: record / import / slice / reverse / 2.x audio","Automate: parameter + solid line confirmed","Send: Export format and/or Cloud / Share To…","Limits used (12.8.7)","After delay: keep / park / Live"],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"The screen recording from 12.9.2 can attach to <strong>capture/edit</strong>. Version is 12.9.5."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Duplicate the list above into Notes or paper.","Fill it for one finished lab Set (12.1–12.4 preferred).","Leave any unused verb as “not used” — do not fake a sample.","Add keep/park/Live after a short delay.","Store the card with the Set name.","Reuse this template on the next sketch without rewriting the headings."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Which six verbs does Gate J name? <strong>Answer:</strong> Setup, capture, edit, sample, automate, send.","Where do you read Note version? <strong>Answer:</strong> Settings → Help (FAQ).","May you invent a house BPM on this card? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Write the number you set and how."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Syllabus Module 11.4 Gate J deliverables","Beatmaking: title, prompt, limitation, intention, delay","Note FAQ: version path; Capture; export/Cloud","Lesson 12.8.7 limits paragraph"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. One complete card for an existing lab Set."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-9-4</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-9-5","title":"12.9.5 — Version number always logged","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.9.5 — Version number always logged","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.9 — Teaching &amp; documentation labs</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Read the installed Note version from Help and write it on every process card and Gate J package."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"FAQ: Settings → <strong>Help</strong> shows the version. Manual §2.5: Help also links videos, manual, KB, release notes, feedback, beta. Auto-update is iOS Settings → App Store if App Updates are on — your logged version can change under you."},{"type":"prose","html":"Version gates you already used: Reverse 1.0.12, 16-bar/groove/Main FX/mapping 1.0.15, Arp/Move/Cloud 8 1.2, Magic Keyboard/poly AT 1.2.1, MIDI Editor pack 1.3, Auto Filter 1.4, Slice 1.7.2, crop/save 1.7.3, audio tracks/Link Audio/Auto Shift/Erosion 2.0.1. Logging the number is how you know which lessons apply."},{"type":"prose","html":"Gate J item 12: version on the notes page. Appendix D is the cheat sheet, not homework to memorize."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Set Library → three dots → <strong>Help</strong>. Write the exact version string.","Add that string to the 12.9.4 card and to any Cloud/export note.","Check iOS App Store → Note to see if an update is waiting. Do not update mid-Gate unless you re-test.","Skim release notes for your number (Help link or ableton.com/en/release-notes/note/).","Write one feature you have and one you do not (for example Slice vs audio tracks).","From memory, say where the version lives."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Where is the version number? <strong>Answer:</strong> Settings → Help (FAQ; Manual §2.5).","Why log it on Gate J? <strong>Answer:</strong> Features are version-gated; syllabus requires it.","Does Cloud store your version for you? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. You write it."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ: version; auto-update","Ableton Note Manual §2.5 Help","Note Release Notes (timeline)","Syllabus Gate J #12; Appendix D"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Five minutes. Version written on the process card and in your lab notebook."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-9-5</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"note-m-12-10-110","code":"12.10","title":"12.10","blurb":"12.10","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"note-l12-10-1","title":"12.10.1 — Rehearse Gate J requirements list","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.10.1 — Rehearse Gate J requirements list","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.10 — Capstone rehearsal week</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Score yourself against the twelve Gate J deliverables before you bounce or upload."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Gate J is a checklist you score from prior sourced facts — not an auto-grader. Syllabus 11.4 deliverables:"},{"type":"list","items":["Note Set with <strong>≥ 4 tracks</strong> (drums, bass, harmony, lead or FX)","<strong>≥ 3 scenes</strong> with intentional density differences","Clips via <strong>Capture</strong> (Fixed <strong>and</strong> Free used at least once)","MIDI Editor polish (timing and velocity intentional)","<strong>≥ 1</strong> user/environmental or imported sample","<strong>≥ 1</strong> captured automation","Key &amp; Scale used intentionally","Audio <strong>export</strong> completed","<strong>Cloud upload or Share To…</strong> completed","Opened in <strong>Live</strong> + <strong>Collect All and Save</strong>","One-page process notes (setup, capture, edit, sample, automate, send)","Note <strong>version</strong> on the notes page"],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"2.x audio track is <strong>not</strong> required unless you later decide it is (syllabus open question). Do not add it to this rehearsal unless you already use it."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Open the intended capstone Set (or pick the strongest lab).","Score 1–12 as yes / no / not yet.","Write the missing items as tomorrow’s dry-run jobs (12.10.2–12.10.4).","Confirm clip origins: at least one Fixed and one Free.","Confirm scenes are not three copies of the same row.","Keep this score sheet; you will update it after each dry run."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Must every clip be captured, never painted? <strong>Answer:</strong> Clips originate via Capture in the process; editor polish is also required.","Is Cloud mandatory if you Share To…? <strong>Answer:</strong> Item 9 is Cloud <strong>or</strong> Share To….","Is a 2.x audio track on the official 12-item list? <strong>Answer:</strong> No."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Syllabus Module 11.4 Capstone requirements","Note FAQ / Manual for each product fact behind the list","Lessons 12.9.4–12.9.5"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Fifteen minutes. Score sheet filled. No export until 12.10.2 unless already done."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-10-1</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-10-2","title":"12.10.2 — Dry run export","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.10.2 — Dry run export","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.10 — Capstone rehearsal week</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Export the capstone Set once, listen all the way through, and fix scene order before Gate J."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Set Settings → <strong>Export Audio</strong>. Greyed if no clips. Scenes render <strong>top to bottom</strong>. Longest clip in a scene sets that scene’s length. <strong>WAV 48 kHz 16-bit</strong> or <strong>M4A 48 kHz 32-bit</strong>. Preview, then <strong>Share</strong> to Files."},{"type":"prose","html":"Dry run means you listen for empty scenes, a verse that is longer than you meant (a 16-bar clip in a “short” row), and tails cut off because the longest clip ended. Fix in Session, export again. This is still Note, not Live Arrangement."},{"type":"prose","html":"Keep the bounce. Gate J item 8 is the completed export."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Show scene numbers. Delete rows you do not want in the bounce.","Export Audio. Choose WAV or M4A. Wait for the preview.","Listen without skipping. Note time stamps of problems.","Fix clips/scenes. Export a second time if needed.","Share the keeper to Files. Name it with the working title + version.","Mark item 8 yes on the 12.10.1 sheet."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What sets a scene’s length in the file? <strong>Answer:</strong> Its longest clip (Manual §10.2).","Why might Export be greyed? <strong>Answer:</strong> No clips in the Set (Manual §5.4).","Does the bounce include Cloud metadata? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. It is audio only."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §5.4; §10.2","Ableton Note.md export formats","Syllabus Gate J #8","Lesson 12.1.7"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Fifteen minutes. One keeper bounce in Files. Score sheet updated."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-10-2</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-10-3","title":"12.10.3 — Dry run Cloud/Share","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.10.3 — Dry run Cloud/Share","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.10 — Capstone rehearsal week</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Land the capstone Set on Cloud <strong>or</strong> as an .ablbundle so item 9 is true before Live day."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Cloud:</strong> same account email as the Live license, Live ≥ 11.2.5 later, internet on, 8-slot ceiling, 100 MB warning. Upload from Settings, banner, or Set Options. Wait — sync can look done on Note before Live has downloaded (Troubleshooting Problems with Note Files)."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Share To…:</strong> .ablbundle for collaborators or a no-Cloud path. AirDrop, Files, messages. Opening the same bundle repeatedly into one folder can confuse macOS filenames (KB: number after extension or lost <code>.ablbundle</code>). Rename or use a fresh folder."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do both if you can. Item 9 needs one. Cloud is not the only copy — keep Projects + the bundle."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Rename the Set if the name is still default. Avoid characters you already know fail Cloud (if a rename is rejected, simplify; {type:'gap'} extracts do not list illegal characters).","Upload to Cloud <strong>or</strong> Share To… Files. Prefer both.","Confirm the Set in the Cloud library section and/or the .ablbundle in Files.","If upload stalls: network, mobile-data toggle, 100 MB samples, Cloud status page (Appendix C).","Do not delete Local.","Mark item 9 yes."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Who can see your Cloud Sets? <strong>Answer:</strong> The same Ableton account on Note/Live/Move/Push — not a collaborator with a different login.","What file does Share To… create? <strong>Answer:</strong> .ablbundle.","Why wait after upload? <strong>Answer:</strong> Live download can still be in progress (Troubleshooting Problems with Note Files)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Note FAQ: Cloud; Share To…","Sharing Note Sets","Note Sets in Ableton Cloud not Appearing in Live","Troubleshooting Problems with Note Files","RN 1.0.6 100 MB"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Ten minutes. Cloud and/or bundle confirmed. Score sheet updated."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-10-3</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-10-4","title":"12.10.4 — Dry run Live Collect All and Save","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.10.4 — Dry run Live Collect All and Save","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.10 — Capstone rehearsal week</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Open the capstone Set in Live 11.2.5+ and Collect All and Save before you change anything else."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Prerequisites: Live <strong>11.2.5+</strong>, same Ableton <strong>email</strong> as Note Cloud, <strong>Show Cloud</strong> in Live Library settings (or open the .ablbundle). All editions work (Trial through Suite, Education)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Open from Live’s browser Cloud folder (double-click .ablbundle or expand .abl). Play. Confirm drums, bass, samples, FX, automation. Then <strong>File → Collect All and Save</strong>. That is Gate J item 10."},{"type":"prose","html":"If Cloud is empty: Appendix C / 13.2.5 — account, Show Cloud, network, status page. If Live warns about file format, RN <strong>1.1.1</strong>: re-save from updated Note; no Live update required."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not add plugins on dry-run day. Do not delete the Cloud slot after collect until you confirm the Live Project plays offline."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Enable Cloud in Note and Show Cloud in Live. Same email.","Open the Set. Listen through the scenes.","Collect All and Save into a named Live Project folder.","Quit Live, disconnect the imagined “Cloud needed” worry: reopen the <strong>local</strong> Live Project and play.","If samples miss, re-upload the Note Set and collect again (Troubleshooting KB).","Mark item 10 yes."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["What Live version is the floor? <strong>Answer:</strong> 11.2.5 (Compatibility; FAQ).","Why Collect All and Save immediately? <strong>Answer:</strong> So samples stay if the Note Set leaves Cloud (Manual §10.1).","Can you open the resulting Live Set in Note to check? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. One-way."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Ableton Note Manual §10.1","Note FAQ: Cloud; Collect All and Save; editions","Note Compatibility","Note Sets in Ableton Cloud not Appearing in Live","RN 1.1.1 format warning","Troubleshooting Problems with Note Files"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Twenty minutes at the computer. Local Live Project plays. Score sheet updated."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-10-4</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-10-5","title":"12.10.5 — Fix gaps found in dry run","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.10.5 — Fix gaps found in dry run","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.10 — Capstone rehearsal week</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Close every “not yet” on the Gate J sheet using only sourced Note (or Collect All and Save) operations."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Work from the score sheet, not from new ideas. Typical gaps:"},{"type":"list","items":["Fewer than 4 tracks or 3 scenes → Add Track / Duplicate scene; stay ≤ 8.","Only Fixed or only Free → Capture the missing mode once and keep the clip.","No editor polish → velocity or timing on one clip.","No sample → record room tone or import WAV/AIFF/M4A/MP3.","No automation → one filter/Delay Add with transport running.","In Key unused → enable and recapture or transpose in-scale.","Export/Cloud/Live missing → repeat 12.10.2–12.10.4.","Process notes / version missing → 12.9.4–12.9.5."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not add Arrangement in Note. Do not add AUv3. If a sample is missing in Live, do not “rebuild in Live” for this gate — fix the Note Set and collect again."},{"type":"prose","html":"Beatmaking: if the idea died during dry run, pick a more memorable lab Set rather than decorating a dead loop."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Open the 12.10.1 sheet. List remaining nos.","Fix them in Note in checklist order (tracks/scenes before send).","Re-export if scenes changed.","Re-upload or re-share if the Set changed after Cloud.","Re-open in Live and Collect All and Save again.","Rescore. You want twelve yeses or a written skip with a sourced reason (no second computer, etc.)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["If you change the Note Set after collect, is the old Live Project current? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Re-open the new transfer and collect again.","Can you skip the sample item? <strong>Answer:</strong> Not for Gate J as written (≥ 1 sample).","What if nothing is memorable? <strong>Answer:</strong> Swap in a better lab Set (Beatmaking memorable test)."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Syllabus Gate J list","Manual Capture, scenes, samples, automation, export, Cloud","Beatmaking: memorable; 80/20","Lessons 12.10.1–12.10.4"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Until the sheet is clean, or one focused hour. Rescore at the end."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-10-5</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"note-l12-10-6","title":"12.10.6 — Final Gate J submission package","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"12.10.6 — Final Gate J submission package","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Level 12 · Module 12.10 — Capstone rehearsal week</em>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"Objective","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Assemble one package that a reviewer can score against the twelve Gate J items without opening your brain."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Instruction","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Package contents (sourced deliverables, not a new file format):"},{"type":"list","items":["Note Set on device (Projects) + Cloud slot and/or <strong>.ablbundle</strong>","Audio export (WAV or M4A)","Live Project after <strong>Collect All and Save</strong>","Process notes page (six verbs + limits paragraph + version)","Optional: 60–90 second screen recording","Score sheet with twelve yeses"],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"There is no in-app “submit Gate J” button. You hand the folder to the course process you already use (Files, AirDrop, LMS). Ableton does not grade this."},{"type":"prose","html":"Name the folder with working title + Note version + date. Keep a Local copy. Cloud remains a transfer slot, not the archive."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Create a folder: <code>GateJ-&lt;title&gt;-&lt;version&gt;</code>.","Put bounce, .ablbundle, process notes, score sheet, optional video in it.","Confirm the Live Project path is written on the notes page.","Play the bounce once more after a delay. If it fails the memorable test, you are submitting a weak sketch — swap now or own it.","Photograph or export the score sheet.","Stop editing the Note Set."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Self-check","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Is Cloud enough as the whole package? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Cloud is transfer; include bounce, notes, collected Live Project.","What twelve items must the notes prove? <strong>Answer:</strong> Syllabus 11.4 list (tracks through version).","Should you keep changing clips after the folder is made? <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Then the bounce and Live Project diverge."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Syllabus Module 11.4 and 12.10 checkpoint","Sharing Note Sets; Manual §10","Beatmaking: delay; memorable"],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Twenty minutes. Folder packed. Hands off the Set."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Syllabus ID: <code>note-l12-10-6</code></em>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
